1
00:00:00,076 --> 00:00:02,476
[Cairo]

2
00:00:02,476 --> 00:00:05,776
[Luxor]

3
00:00:05,776 --> 00:00:07,250
[Finally, WANGGEOZ arrive]

4
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:09,909
[at Giftun Island in Hurghada]

5
00:00:09,909 --> 00:00:11,977
The title of this mission is…

6
00:00:11,977 --> 00:00:14,277
"Conversations with the Ancients".

7
00:00:14,277 --> 00:00:16,276
- "Conversations with the Ancients"
- "Conversations with the Ancients"?

8
00:00:19,009 --> 00:00:21,568
[Find the ancient hieroglyphs]

9
00:00:21,568 --> 00:00:23,377
[scattered all over the island]
Wow!

10
00:00:23,377 --> 00:00:25,001
So this is it!
It's this kind of thing!

11
00:00:25,001 --> 00:00:28,367
[Decoding the clues to collect the letters]

12
00:00:29,076 --> 00:00:30,675
[and combining them into a complete word]
Eagle.

13
00:00:30,675 --> 00:00:31,876
"A",

14
00:00:31,876 --> 00:00:33,087
"M", "R"…

15
00:00:33,087 --> 00:00:34,143
"C"!

16
00:00:34,143 --> 00:00:35,910
[Bring the item that matches the word]
Did you bring it?

17
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:37,776
- Pencil.
- Incorrect!

18
00:00:37,776 --> 00:00:39,382
Is it related to the word you found?

19
00:00:39,382 --> 00:00:42,109
Where would you get that?

20
00:00:42,109 --> 00:00:45,077
[Meanwhile, here are the letters revealed so far]

21
00:00:45,077 --> 00:00:49,110
[A, L, M, R, C, E/Y]

22
00:00:49,110 --> 00:00:50,980
[And]

23
00:00:50,980 --> 00:00:52,610
[Appearing before Lee Teuk]
Wait, what's this?

24
00:00:52,610 --> 00:00:54,364
[A suspicious Z]
This looks kinda fishy.

25
00:00:54,364 --> 00:00:55,965
You have a "Z"?

26
00:00:55,965 --> 00:00:57,868
- This one is that.
- What?

27
00:00:57,868 --> 00:00:59,676
- To trick people…!
- Oh, you're trying to trick people.

28
00:00:59,676 --> 00:01:01,877
[The fake Z Lee Teuk casually dropped]
1, 2, 3!

29
00:01:01,877 --> 00:01:02,534
Nice!

30
00:01:02,534 --> 00:01:04,073
[Engulfing WANGGEOZ in no time...]
Oh, "Z".

31
00:01:04,073 --> 00:01:05,842
So, there's a "Z".

32
00:01:05,842 --> 00:01:07,577
[Z???]
Oh? Oh?

33
00:01:07,577 --> 00:01:09,802
There aren't many words with "Z" in them…

34
00:01:09,802 --> 00:01:11,177
[They start chasing
an answer that doesn't exist]

35
00:01:11,177 --> 00:01:13,968
[The chaos created by Lee Teuk's Z]
What's this? Wait, what was that?

36
00:01:13,968 --> 00:01:17,968
[Today, the outcome will be revealed]
I really can't trust Lee Teuk! This is driving me nuts.

37
00:01:19,743 --> 00:01:20,776
[Lee Teuk]

38
00:01:21,209 --> 00:01:22,376
[Shin Dong]

39
00:01:22,376 --> 00:01:23,576
[Dawn]

40
00:01:23,576 --> 00:01:24,943
[Johnny]

41
00:01:24,943 --> 00:01:26,209
[Kim Yo Han]

42
00:01:26,209 --> 00:01:27,176
[Ji Sung]

43
00:01:35,305 --> 00:01:36,306
I found 6!

44
00:01:36,306 --> 00:01:37,577
- Seriously?
- Yeah.

45
00:01:37,577 --> 00:01:39,077
Then let's show
each other just one letter.

46
00:01:39,077 --> 00:01:40,879
- One by one, okay.
- I have… 1, 2, 3, 4, 5...

47
00:01:40,879 --> 00:01:41,769
[Shin Dong's Collection Status: A, L, M, R, C]
Oh! I have 6 too.

48
00:01:41,769 --> 00:01:42,610
[Lee Teuk's Collection Status: Z, A, EY, L, M]
Oh, okay then.

49
00:01:42,610 --> 00:01:44,377
[Sharing everything after 20 years of trust]
Lee Teuk, then let's just open it.

50
00:01:44,377 --> 00:01:44,977
Oh, just open it?

51
00:01:44,977 --> 00:01:45,977
- Let's just open it completely together.
- Okay.

52
00:01:45,977 --> 00:01:47,149
- 1, 2, 3!
- 1, 2, 3!

53
00:01:47,780 --> 00:01:49,080
[Lee Teuk's Collection Status: Z, A, EY, L, M, C]
[Shin Dong's Collection Status: A, L, M, R, C, EY]

54
00:01:49,080 --> 00:01:49,881
Oh, wait!

55
00:01:49,881 --> 00:01:51,867
Lee Teuk, what's this?
Are you sure you have 6?

56
00:01:51,867 --> 00:01:53,043
Isn't this one?

57
00:01:53,043 --> 00:01:54,944
Lee Teuk, you have a "Z"?

58
00:01:54,944 --> 00:01:56,977
- This one is that.
- What?

59
00:01:56,977 --> 00:01:58,589
- To trick people…!
- Oh, you're trying to trick people.

60
00:01:58,589 --> 00:02:00,590
[Lee Teuk's Collection Status: Z, A, EY, L, M, C]
This and this one are definitely real.

61
00:02:00,590 --> 00:02:02,932
[Shin Dong's Collection Status: A, L, M, R, C, EY]
Lee Teuk, you have everything I have!

62
00:02:02,932 --> 00:02:04,901
You know less than I do!

63
00:02:04,901 --> 00:02:05,835
Is there anything missing?

64
00:02:05,835 --> 00:02:07,009
Hurry and look.

65
00:02:07,009 --> 00:02:09,677
What's this? Was there an "E"?

66
00:02:09,677 --> 00:02:10,787
"E" is this.

67
00:02:10,787 --> 00:02:11,841
Yeah, so there is an "E"?

68
00:02:11,841 --> 00:02:12,876
[CARAMEL]
Is it... "CARAMEL"?

69
00:02:12,876 --> 00:02:14,945
Oh! Oh!

70
00:02:14,945 --> 00:02:17,910
[Shin Dong's Collection Status: A, L, M, R, C, EY]
[C, A, R, M, E, L]

71
00:02:17,910 --> 00:02:19,877
If it's "CARAMEL",
there should be two "A"s, Lee Teuk.

72
00:02:19,877 --> 00:02:21,276
Then it's not.

73
00:02:21,276 --> 00:02:24,020
What item is there for a camel?

74
00:02:24,020 --> 00:02:25,376
[Camel]
"Camel".

75
00:02:25,376 --> 00:02:26,743
Oh!

76
00:02:26,743 --> 00:02:28,444
- Lee Teuk, I think it's "CAMEL".
- Oh!

77
00:02:28,444 --> 00:02:30,126
I've been looking for a camel
since earlier, and there are none!

78
00:02:30,126 --> 00:02:32,395
[A little excited]
We're supposed to bring something related.

79
00:02:32,395 --> 00:02:34,030
- Shin Dong.
- Yeah?

80
00:02:34,030 --> 00:02:36,230
Don't you think it's "water"?

81
00:02:36,700 --> 00:02:39,667
Camels store water here.

82
00:02:40,337 --> 00:02:42,137
- Let's go quietly and try it out.
- Yeah.

83
00:02:43,076 --> 00:02:46,976
[The two veterans
sneak around searching for water]

84
00:02:48,245 --> 00:02:50,044
Shin Dong, did you find anything?

85
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:52,077
[Trying it out even if he gets nothing!]
I'm just gonna try it!

86
00:02:52,077 --> 00:02:53,134
I'm not sure, but I'm gonna try it!

87
00:02:53,134 --> 00:02:54,718
[For security, one person enters at a time]
Okay, please come in alone.

88
00:02:54,718 --> 00:02:57,084
Step back, step back, please.

89
00:02:57,084 --> 00:02:58,378
Please step back.

90
00:02:58,378 --> 00:03:00,476
[Water]
Answer! "Water."

91
00:03:00,476 --> 00:03:01,773
Please say it in English.

92
00:03:01,773 --> 00:03:02,686
Water.

93
00:03:02,686 --> 00:03:04,710
Incorrect.

94
00:03:04,710 --> 00:03:06,643
Wait, really?

95
00:03:07,135 --> 00:03:08,409
- It's not, it's not.
- It's not, it's not, it's not.

96
00:03:08,409 --> 00:03:10,999
[Player substitution]
Oh, because...! Because…!

97
00:03:10,999 --> 00:03:12,977
It's an empty bottle,
but pretend there's "water" in it.

98
00:03:12,977 --> 00:03:14,544
[Super fail]
It's not?

99
00:03:14,544 --> 00:03:16,610
- I think I'm starting to get this game.
- Oh, really?

100
00:03:16,610 --> 00:03:18,677
So we're supposed to
find something related to this.

101
00:03:18,677 --> 00:03:21,210
[Bring an item]
That completed word is here in this place.

102
00:03:21,210 --> 00:03:22,444
[that's related to the completed word]
You have to bring that item here.

103
00:03:22,444 --> 00:03:26,443
[What on earth is hidden on this island?]
Something related… Water.

104
00:03:28,251 --> 00:03:29,853
Oh!

105
00:03:29,853 --> 00:03:32,110
Wait! How am I supposed
to bring that over there?

106
00:03:32,110 --> 00:03:33,277
You have to bring it here.

107
00:03:33,277 --> 00:03:34,277
But I can't bring it here.

108
00:03:34,277 --> 00:03:37,712
- Then, it must not be the answer.
- Oh! Here it is!

109
00:03:38,261 --> 00:03:39,371
This!

110
00:03:41,309 --> 00:03:42,777
A "cactus!"

111
00:03:42,777 --> 00:03:43,977
What is that in English?

112
00:03:43,977 --> 00:03:44,877
"Cactus"!

113
00:03:44,877 --> 00:03:47,610
You must've combined
the letters together, no?

114
00:03:47,610 --> 00:03:49,677
[Aloe]
Aloe.

115
00:03:49,677 --> 00:03:50,777
["Cactus" is cactus]
Incorrect.

116
00:03:50,777 --> 00:03:52,256
[A nice wrong answer]
Oh, it must be similar!

117
00:03:53,276 --> 00:03:55,537
Oh! Camera?

118
00:03:59,149 --> 00:04:00,455
This!

119
00:04:00,455 --> 00:04:01,417
[Answer: "CAMERA"]
Please tell us.

120
00:04:01,417 --> 00:04:02,519
A camera!

121
00:04:02,519 --> 00:04:06,677
Shin Dong did the exact
same thing 10 minutes ago.

122
00:04:06,677 --> 00:04:08,243
Ugh, Shin Dong!

123
00:04:08,243 --> 00:04:11,176
[Booster up again]

124
00:04:11,809 --> 00:04:15,009
[Basically a flying squirrel]

125
00:04:15,009 --> 00:04:17,243
[Searching]

126
00:04:23,173 --> 00:04:24,898
[DAWN's Collection Status: A, EY, L, Z]

127
00:04:24,898 --> 00:04:26,877
Wait, that's…!

128
00:04:26,877 --> 00:04:30,210
[Got the letter "C"!]
It's a different one! "C"!

129
00:04:30,210 --> 00:04:34,076
[DAWN's Collection Status: A, EY, L, Z, C]

130
00:04:34,076 --> 00:04:38,776
[Super Big Johnny appears between the parasols]

131
00:04:40,643 --> 00:04:42,377
It's so tiring, right?

132
00:04:42,377 --> 00:04:44,243
I'm seriously struggling.

133
00:04:45,109 --> 00:04:47,486
[Here and there]

134
00:04:49,595 --> 00:04:50,968
Wow, no way.

135
00:04:51,434 --> 00:04:53,870
Of course, I couldn't find it
because it's placed like this!

136
00:04:53,870 --> 00:04:56,740
[After Ji Sung looked at it earlier,]

137
00:04:56,740 --> 00:04:59,672
[he hung it up in a rush and left]

138
00:05:02,512 --> 00:05:04,247
[Found his 2nd hieroglyph, the bird]

139
00:05:04,247 --> 00:05:05,109
A bird.

140
00:05:05,109 --> 00:05:06,182
[Johnny's Collection Status: M, A]

141
00:05:06,182 --> 00:05:09,016
[Decoded the bird image and got "A"]

142
00:05:09,016 --> 00:05:09,877
Should I try to guess?

143
00:05:09,877 --> 00:05:12,816
[PYRAMID]
From what I see, it's "PYRAMID".

144
00:05:12,816 --> 00:05:15,015
I only saw "M" and "A," though.

145
00:05:17,843 --> 00:05:18,777
[Johnny's Collection Status: M, A, C]

146
00:05:18,777 --> 00:05:21,978
["C" obtained, so it's not "Pyramid"]
Wait, this is a "C".

147
00:05:21,978 --> 00:05:23,084
"C", "M", "A".

148
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:26,476
Ji Sung! I think it's that.

149
00:05:26,476 --> 00:05:28,677
[Sharing the good news he got from Lee Teuk]
But I actually know the letters, up to "Z"!

150
00:05:28,677 --> 00:05:30,140
I know a few more letters.

151
00:05:30,140 --> 00:05:31,877
[Tell me what got added]
Please share them.

152
00:05:31,877 --> 00:05:34,277
If you share,
I'll quickly pass it along to you.

153
00:05:34,277 --> 00:05:35,890
- There's a "Z"?
- There's apparently a "Z".

154
00:05:35,890 --> 00:05:36,977
[Shin Dong's Collection Status: A, L, M, R, C, EY]
I shared letters with Lee Teuk.

155
00:05:36,977 --> 00:05:38,380
[Ji Sung's Collection Status: A, L, M, R, C, Z]
He lied to you.

156
00:05:38,380 --> 00:05:39,583
- Seriously?
- He lied.

157
00:05:39,583 --> 00:05:41,083
Then, I think Lee Teuk

158
00:05:41,083 --> 00:05:43,662
- is gonna traumatize me for life.
- He lied.

159
00:05:43,662 --> 00:05:44,810
Wow, wait.

160
00:05:44,810 --> 00:05:47,156
Ji Sung, you survived because of me!

161
00:05:47,156 --> 00:05:49,776
There's no "Z".

162
00:05:49,776 --> 00:05:52,144
So, what exactly
is this English word?

163
00:05:52,144 --> 00:05:53,677
Camera... Isn't it "CAMERA"?

164
00:05:53,677 --> 00:05:54,644
It's not "CAMERA".

165
00:05:54,644 --> 00:05:57,333
What is it? "CARAMEL", maybe?

166
00:05:57,333 --> 00:05:59,961
Ji Sung, did you get something wrong?
Like, the "C" or something?

167
00:05:59,961 --> 00:06:03,139
Definitely not. I'm 100% sure about this.

168
00:06:03,139 --> 00:06:06,643
There are many kinds of birds.
You could've gotten them confused.

169
00:06:06,643 --> 00:06:09,110
Did you get the drawings correctly?

170
00:06:09,110 --> 00:06:10,980
[3 bird drawings: A, M, W]

171
00:06:10,980 --> 00:06:12,756
- I'm gonna double-check.
- Yeah.

172
00:06:14,851 --> 00:06:16,786
I seriously have no clue.

173
00:06:16,786 --> 00:06:19,194
At this time,
you'd think I would've found it.

174
00:06:20,056 --> 00:06:22,678
But I'm bad at English.
What do I do?

175
00:06:22,678 --> 00:06:24,844
Ji Sung, I have no idea at all.

176
00:06:24,844 --> 00:06:27,311
- How many did you find?
- Me?

177
00:06:27,311 --> 00:06:28,578
5!

178
00:06:28,578 --> 00:06:30,244
You found a lot!

179
00:06:30,244 --> 00:06:32,015
But I don't know English.

180
00:06:32,015 --> 00:06:35,411
Yo Han, you're in
the same boat as me right now.

181
00:06:35,411 --> 00:06:38,078
- I just can't piece it together.
- I just can't piece it together.

182
00:06:38,078 --> 00:06:40,977
[Frustrated]

183
00:06:41,643 --> 00:06:44,844
[First, off to check the birds]

184
00:06:44,844 --> 00:06:46,611
Ugh! I'm so tired!

185
00:06:46,611 --> 00:06:48,414
[A groan involuntarily escapes]
Oh, I'm so tired.

186
00:06:48,414 --> 00:06:50,210
There was something here earlier.

187
00:06:52,036 --> 00:06:54,309
[3 bird drawings: A, M, W]
Yeah, it's this one.

188
00:06:54,309 --> 00:06:56,115
This is… Let's look.

189
00:06:59,836 --> 00:07:01,496
[This bird is definitely "A"]
It's "A". Yeah, yeah. It's "A", it's "A".

190
00:07:01,496 --> 00:07:02,689
It's not "W".

191
00:07:02,689 --> 00:07:04,343
It's not "A"… I mean, it's not "W".

192
00:07:04,343 --> 00:07:06,770
I kept running! I kept searching!

193
00:07:06,770 --> 00:07:09,111
I would find the letters,
then tell the members.

194
00:07:09,111 --> 00:07:12,042
And then I'd ask them about it too.

195
00:07:12,042 --> 00:07:14,408
That's when I realized
I was being way too honest.

196
00:07:15,712 --> 00:07:18,110
I'm losing it.

197
00:07:18,110 --> 00:07:20,680
This is driving me nuts.

198
00:07:21,310 --> 00:07:22,210
[Fumbling]

199
00:07:22,210 --> 00:07:24,544
Where the heck are my sunglasses?

200
00:07:24,544 --> 00:07:26,978
[You're holding them in your hand...]
Oh, shoot. They're here.

201
00:07:26,978 --> 00:07:30,660
[He begins begging the cameraman]
Can you please give me one little hint?

202
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:33,496
I seriously can't find it.

203
00:07:33,496 --> 00:07:35,465
Just one…! The very first letter!

204
00:07:35,465 --> 00:07:37,565
Oh, seriously! Please…!

205
00:07:37,976 --> 00:07:40,370
[Q. What does English mean to Yo Han?]

206
00:07:40,370 --> 00:07:42,511
I need to be reborn.

207
00:07:42,511 --> 00:07:45,444
I should've quit sports sooner.

208
00:07:45,444 --> 00:07:48,979
Yo Han, why did you
only do sports when you were little?

209
00:07:48,979 --> 00:07:51,310
You should've studied English!

210
00:07:51,310 --> 00:07:52,677
- Yo Han!
- Yes?

211
00:07:52,677 --> 00:07:56,210
Let's team up!
Two heads are better than one.

212
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:59,344
Oh… I… I mean… The letters…

213
00:07:59,344 --> 00:08:01,144
- How many did you find?
- I found 5.

214
00:08:01,144 --> 00:08:01,991
I also have 5.

215
00:08:01,991 --> 00:08:03,544
But I can't figure out
how to put them together.

216
00:08:03,544 --> 00:08:04,811
Let's figure it out together.

217
00:08:04,811 --> 00:08:07,836
[Shin Dong's target this time is Yo Han]
You might have some letters I don't.

218
00:08:07,836 --> 00:08:09,503
I'll tell you right away.

219
00:08:09,503 --> 00:08:11,804
[Shin Dong's Collection Status: A, L, M, R, C, EY]
I have them like this.

220
00:08:11,804 --> 00:08:12,937
Quickly sit down.

221
00:08:12,937 --> 00:08:14,637
[Peeking]
It's better if we team up quickly.

222
00:08:14,637 --> 00:08:16,223
[Yo Han's Collection Status: A, M, L, C, EY]

223
00:08:16,223 --> 00:08:18,252
"A", "L"…

224
00:08:18,252 --> 00:08:19,576
"M", "C"…

225
00:08:19,576 --> 00:08:20,541
"C", "R"…

226
00:08:20,541 --> 00:08:21,577
"Ey".

227
00:08:21,577 --> 00:08:23,746
- There's a "Y"?
- "E" or "Y".

228
00:08:23,746 --> 00:08:25,161
- There's either "E" or "Y"?
- Yes.

229
00:08:25,161 --> 00:08:26,675
"E" or "Y".

230
00:08:26,675 --> 00:08:28,342
[Double-checking "E/Y" with Lee Teuk and Yo Han]
I found this.

231
00:08:28,342 --> 00:08:30,460
Really? Then it is 6 letters.

232
00:08:31,526 --> 00:08:33,738
[If 6 are found, then the total letters are…]
Oh, but I'm not…

233
00:08:33,738 --> 00:08:35,444
- I'm not good at English.
- Same here.

234
00:08:35,444 --> 00:08:37,377
[The 2nd half of "Conversations with the Ancients"]
Geez, what could it be?

235
00:08:37,377 --> 00:08:38,836
This is not easy.

236
00:08:38,836 --> 00:08:40,210
I'm in big trouble.

237
00:08:40,210 --> 00:08:41,551
[Announcement]

238
00:08:41,551 --> 00:08:43,777
- A message just came from HQ.
- What did they say?

239
00:08:43,777 --> 00:08:46,032
The total number of letters is 7.

240
00:08:46,032 --> 00:08:47,439
There are 7 letters?

241
00:08:47,439 --> 00:08:49,166
The total is 7 letters.

242
00:08:49,166 --> 00:08:50,752
- 7 letters?
- Yes, 7 letters.

243
00:08:50,752 --> 00:08:53,151
- What did you say?
- The total number of letters is 7.

244
00:08:53,151 --> 00:08:54,944
- There are 7 letters?
- 7 letters?

245
00:08:54,944 --> 00:08:57,676
[Ancient language = 7 letters]
Where did they all find them?

246
00:08:57,676 --> 00:09:00,977
[Ji Sung found 5 letters]
Wait, hold on a sec.

247
00:09:00,977 --> 00:09:02,144
[Shin Dong and Yo Han found 6 letters]
But since it's "E" or "Y",

248
00:09:02,144 --> 00:09:04,247
couldn't both "E" and "Y" be included?

249
00:09:04,247 --> 00:09:05,444
Is that how it goes?

250
00:09:05,444 --> 00:09:07,543
[DAWN believes he has 5 letters, including Z]
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6.

251
00:09:07,543 --> 00:09:09,011
[DAWN's Collection Status: A, EY, L, Z, C]
I have 6.

252
00:09:09,011 --> 00:09:10,273
[Lee Teuk found 5 letters]
But where did they all find them?

253
00:09:10,273 --> 00:09:11,677
[Lee Teuk's Collection Status: Z, A, EY, L, M, C]
I only found one.

254
00:09:11,677 --> 00:09:14,544
[Johnny found the least]
"C", "M", "A". So that means there are 4 more.

255
00:09:14,544 --> 00:09:15,634
[Current letter status]

256
00:09:15,634 --> 00:09:18,027
[Tied for 1st: Shin Dong / Yo Han]
[Tied for 3rd: Lee Teuk / Ji Sung]

257
00:09:18,027 --> 00:09:20,854
[5th: DAWN]
[6th: Johnny]

258
00:09:20,854 --> 00:09:21,943
- Hey, Shin Dong.
- Yeah?

259
00:09:21,943 --> 00:09:24,211
They said you and I both said the same answer.

260
00:09:24,211 --> 00:09:25,251
[SUPER JUNIOR became one through "CAMERA"]
Oh, really?

261
00:09:25,251 --> 00:09:27,010
- You did "CAMERA" too?
- Yeah.

262
00:09:27,710 --> 00:09:29,936
(Camera...????)
This is so hard. I can't do this.

263
00:09:29,936 --> 00:09:33,154
I have 6 letters,
but I can't piece them together.

264
00:09:33,154 --> 00:09:34,261
It's so…

265
00:09:34,261 --> 00:09:37,153
Are we too obsessed with that?

266
00:09:37,153 --> 00:09:40,876
But don't they want us
to put the letters together?

267
00:09:40,876 --> 00:09:43,226
Bring something?
Where is it?

268
00:09:43,226 --> 00:09:44,895
Yeah, they want us to bring something.

269
00:09:44,895 --> 00:09:47,461
I brought them 3 items,
and they were all wrong.

270
00:09:49,332 --> 00:09:51,147
You took 3 items?

271
00:09:51,147 --> 00:09:52,068
[Even after finding 6 out of the 7 letters]
Where could it be?

272
00:09:52,068 --> 00:09:54,394
Should we just grab something and try?

273
00:09:55,743 --> 00:09:57,238
[No idea...]

274
00:09:57,238 --> 00:09:58,864
Ugh, where is it?

275
00:09:58,864 --> 00:10:00,843
This doesn't feel right.

276
00:10:00,843 --> 00:10:01,978
[Taking advantage
of the confusion...]

277
00:10:01,978 --> 00:10:03,377
Oh, what? This…

278
00:10:04,476 --> 00:10:06,356
[Shin Dong sneaks away]

279
00:10:06,356 --> 00:10:08,063
Where is this?

280
00:10:09,758 --> 00:10:11,333
[Suspicious]
Where is this?

281
00:10:11,333 --> 00:10:13,527
Oh! You seem like
you're acting right now!

282
00:10:13,527 --> 00:10:15,780
[Ignoring Yo Han's suspicion]
Oh! You seem like you're acting right now!

283
00:10:15,780 --> 00:10:16,860
I think he found something.

284
00:10:16,860 --> 00:10:18,576
But where is this?

285
00:10:18,576 --> 00:10:20,976
[Entering HQ]

286
00:10:21,376 --> 00:10:23,144
Answer! Ramesses?

287
00:10:23,144 --> 00:10:24,200
You have to bring it here

288
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,776
Where is Ramesses?

289
00:10:25,776 --> 00:10:28,443
If you can't bring it,
it's not the answer.

290
00:10:28,443 --> 00:10:30,744
This is "Y" or "E", right?

291
00:10:30,744 --> 00:10:33,543
Are both letters included?

292
00:10:33,543 --> 00:10:34,854
It's one of the two.

293
00:10:34,854 --> 00:10:35,943
One of the two.

294
00:10:35,943 --> 00:10:38,252
[Shin Dong's Collection Status: A, L, M, R, C, EY]
Oh, that's why it seemed so weird to me.

295
00:10:38,252 --> 00:10:39,777
So it's one of the two…

296
00:10:39,777 --> 00:10:42,911
[You got this, Captain Shin!]

297
00:10:42,911 --> 00:10:44,358
Wow.

298
00:10:44,358 --> 00:10:46,377
I really suck at English.

299
00:10:46,377 --> 00:10:48,144
[It's a word chosen based on everyone's level…]
Just because your English isn't great

300
00:10:48,144 --> 00:10:50,511
doesn't mean you can't solve it.

301
00:10:50,511 --> 00:10:52,644
Can I please use AI just once?

302
00:10:52,644 --> 00:10:54,544
[The one who uses modern civilization]
Then you will beg for eternity.

303
00:10:54,544 --> 00:10:56,244
[will beg for eternity]
It's written on the first page.

304
00:10:56,244 --> 00:10:57,939
I think I can beg
for the rest of my life...

305
00:10:57,939 --> 00:10:59,343
Then, can I use it?

306
00:10:59,343 --> 00:11:03,243
[Sacrificing his life for the status mission]
I want to beg forever.

307
00:11:03,243 --> 00:11:04,608
Wanna know what's even funnier?

308
00:11:04,608 --> 00:11:07,018
[Got all the letters from someone else]
I got these letters by making deals with everyone.

309
00:11:07,018 --> 00:11:10,964
[Ultimate efficiency]
I haven't seen a single drawing yet.

310
00:11:11,443 --> 00:11:14,676
[After gathering lots of info, he leaves HQ]
Sigh…

311
00:11:15,276 --> 00:11:18,340
[Yo Han, who missed his chance to study English]
First, you gotta know what this is to find it.

312
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:19,666
[Yo Han's Collection Status: A, M, L, C, EY, R]
I don't know what it is,

313
00:11:19,666 --> 00:11:21,305
so how am I supposed to find it?

314
00:11:24,310 --> 00:11:26,296
Please give me your "CAMERA".

315
00:11:26,296 --> 00:11:27,882
I'm gonna take the camera over.

316
00:11:28,276 --> 00:11:32,143
[Remembered what the older members said earlier]
Please give me your camera.

317
00:11:33,352 --> 00:11:36,711
[Camera]
Is it this?

318
00:11:36,711 --> 00:11:37,544
Incorrect.

319
00:11:37,544 --> 00:11:39,476
- It wasn't a camera.
- Please return it.

320
00:11:39,476 --> 00:11:41,310
Sorry about that.

321
00:11:41,310 --> 00:11:44,843
[The older members
even said they failed with it…]

322
00:11:44,843 --> 00:11:47,244
[Deep in English anxiety]
I'm bad at English! What do I do about this?

323
00:11:47,244 --> 00:11:48,111
[Meanwhile, Ji Sung]

324
00:11:48,111 --> 00:11:51,843
(Still worried about the English)
[Ji Sung's Collection Status: A, L, M, R, C, Z]

325
00:11:52,510 --> 00:11:54,456
(Striding forward)

326
00:11:54,456 --> 00:11:55,443
I…

327
00:11:55,443 --> 00:11:57,243
Ca... camera...!

328
00:11:58,837 --> 00:11:59,676
Camera!

329
00:11:59,676 --> 00:12:01,931
[The 4th "CAMERA" challenger]

330
00:12:01,931 --> 00:12:03,466
Camera!

331
00:12:03,466 --> 00:12:06,136
[From the very first "CAMERA" challenger,]
Camera!

332
00:12:06,136 --> 00:12:07,537
[the members all connected with the same answer]
This!

333
00:12:07,537 --> 00:12:08,836
- Please say the answer
- Camera!

334
00:12:08,836 --> 00:12:10,054
- Did you bring it?
- Yes.

335
00:12:10,054 --> 00:12:10,711
Incorrect.

336
00:12:10,711 --> 00:12:12,430
Three people have already guessed "CAMERA".

337
00:12:12,430 --> 00:12:13,257
- Really?
- Yes

338
00:12:13,257 --> 00:12:16,310
There were 3 people smarter than me?

339
00:12:17,354 --> 00:12:18,944
[Person smarter than Ji Sung #1]
Please give me one hint.

340
00:12:18,944 --> 00:12:21,142
[Begging for a hint]
Just tell me the first letter.

341
00:12:21,142 --> 00:12:22,176
You can't?

342
00:12:22,176 --> 00:12:23,843
You're almost there.

343
00:12:23,843 --> 00:12:26,039
I'm not there at all.

344
00:12:26,039 --> 00:12:28,721
[Person smarter than Ji Sung #2]
Seriously, I'll give you 50,000 won!

345
00:12:28,721 --> 00:12:30,160
[Offering a bribe]
Just one hint.

346
00:12:30,160 --> 00:12:32,044
[Frustrated on both sides]
Combine them all together and bring it here.

347
00:12:32,044 --> 00:12:34,320
I'm telling you, I can't combine them!

348
00:12:35,043 --> 00:12:36,925
- Please go back.
- I can't combine them together.

349
00:12:36,925 --> 00:12:38,050
Want to team up and try combining these with me?

350
00:12:38,050 --> 00:12:40,644
Then that means someone scammed you.

351
00:12:40,644 --> 00:12:41,446
I got scammed?

352
00:12:41,446 --> 00:12:43,843
There's a high chance
you were scammed by someone.

353
00:12:43,843 --> 00:12:45,710
[Dashing]

354
00:12:46,710 --> 00:12:48,410
- Shin Dong!
- Yeah?

355
00:12:48,410 --> 00:12:49,844
- I just went and checked.
- Yeah?

356
00:12:49,844 --> 00:12:53,177
We didn't find the letters ourselves,
but got them from the members, right?

357
00:12:53,177 --> 00:12:56,144
They said there was a scammer!

358
00:12:56,144 --> 00:12:57,653
The scammer was you, Lee Teuk.

359
00:12:57,653 --> 00:12:59,157
- Oh, that's me?
- Yeah.

360
00:12:59,157 --> 00:13:01,443
- Am I the only one?
- Yeah. The "Z".

361
00:13:01,443 --> 00:13:04,244
[The one and only scammer, Lee Teuk]
So, it's you, Lee Teuk.

362
00:13:04,244 --> 00:13:07,411
I went down there…

363
00:13:07,411 --> 00:13:08,999
Oh, what's this?

364
00:13:08,999 --> 00:13:10,244
This is suspicious.

365
00:13:10,244 --> 00:13:12,831
- On the bed, there was a big "Z" written on it.
- Come on.

366
00:13:12,831 --> 00:13:15,677
[The "Z" was written everywhere]
But it was written on all the beds there.

367
00:13:15,677 --> 00:13:19,277
[First victim: DAWN]
1, 2, 3!

368
00:13:19,277 --> 00:13:22,176
[Second victim: Ji Sung]
1, 2, 3!

369
00:13:22,905 --> 00:13:24,477
So to intentionally trick them,

370
00:13:24,477 --> 00:13:26,344
[The confession diary of a scammer]
I found an "A", covered it up,

371
00:13:26,344 --> 00:13:28,211
and then showed them one by one!

372
00:13:28,211 --> 00:13:30,657
[Meanwhile, Lee Teuk's victims]
DAWN, I can't figure it out as I'm bad at English.

373
00:13:30,657 --> 00:13:32,289
I think I found a lot of the letters, though.

374
00:13:32,289 --> 00:13:34,354
Let's share, Ji Sung.

375
00:13:34,354 --> 00:13:37,494
I've shared way too much.
Everyone probably knows already.

376
00:13:37,494 --> 00:13:38,361
Oh, really?

377
00:13:38,361 --> 00:13:40,746
- What should I do?
- Then, let's solve it together.

378
00:13:40,746 --> 00:13:42,077
But one thing I don't trust is…

379
00:13:42,077 --> 00:13:44,277
[Victim 1]
I traded one letter with Lee Teuk.

380
00:13:44,277 --> 00:13:45,201
He might be lying.

381
00:13:45,201 --> 00:13:46,670
[Victim 2]
I also swapped one with Lee Teuk.

382
00:13:46,670 --> 00:13:47,671
[When suspicions turn into reality]
What did you trade?

383
00:13:47,671 --> 00:13:49,744
Lee Teuk gave me "Z".

384
00:13:49,744 --> 00:13:50,835
That's right.

385
00:13:50,835 --> 00:13:52,340
- It must be a lie.
- I think it's weird.

386
00:13:52,340 --> 00:13:53,578
[The "Z" just feels suspicious]
I don't know about this.

387
00:13:53,578 --> 00:13:56,256
[Ji Sung's Collection Status: A, L, M, R, C, Z]
I'll show you mine. These aren't it, but it's this.

388
00:13:56,256 --> 00:13:57,543
- What? This?
- Yeah.

389
00:13:57,543 --> 00:13:59,438
[DAWN's Collection Status: A, EY, L, Z, C]
I got this one.

390
00:13:59,438 --> 00:14:01,061
[Ji Sung's Collection Status: A, L, M, R, C, Z, EY]
The "E" is… Oh?

391
00:14:01,061 --> 00:14:02,626
[DAWN's letters: A, EY, L, Z, C, M, R]
Oh, you didn't find this one!

392
00:14:02,626 --> 00:14:03,631
[Got "E/Y"]
So it's "E" and "Y"?

393
00:14:03,631 --> 00:14:04,761
Yeah. Wait a second.

394
00:14:04,761 --> 00:14:08,077
I think we can actually do this.

395
00:14:08,077 --> 00:14:09,254
[6 out of 7 letters is worth trying to figure out]
Ji Sung, let's make a plan.

396
00:14:09,254 --> 00:14:10,948
Wait, from what I see here…

397
00:14:10,948 --> 00:14:13,353
- What if…
- Prince, prince, prince! Pauper, pauper, pauper!

398
00:14:13,353 --> 00:14:14,677
- 1, 2, 3, 4.
- Okay.

399
00:14:14,677 --> 00:14:16,830
Since "A" is usually a vowel…

400
00:14:16,830 --> 00:14:18,743
"A" and "E" are vowels.

401
00:14:20,136 --> 00:14:22,028
Isn't it this?
"CAMEL"?

402
00:14:22,028 --> 00:14:24,960
[Letter count doesn't match]
Isn't it this? "CAMEL"?

403
00:14:25,343 --> 00:14:27,162
- Oh!
- Are we allowed to team up?

404
00:14:27,162 --> 00:14:29,742
[Mr. John Jun Suh suddenly appears]
Are we allowed to team up?

405
00:14:29,742 --> 00:14:30,910
(Has 3 letters)

406
00:14:31,710 --> 00:14:33,351
[Happy to see his NCT member]
But Johnny!

407
00:14:33,351 --> 00:14:34,944
- Johnny, but…
- Can we team up?

408
00:14:34,944 --> 00:14:36,044
But, well…

409
00:14:36,044 --> 00:14:37,544
Among the English words…

410
00:14:37,544 --> 00:14:39,797
No, don't tell Johnny,
who's good at English.

411
00:14:39,797 --> 00:14:41,176
That…

412
00:14:41,176 --> 00:14:45,277
[The language barrier]

413
00:14:45,277 --> 00:14:48,011
Johnny, but… Um… Wait.

414
00:14:48,011 --> 00:14:49,544
[DAWN and Ji Sung are wary of Johnny]
I've got quite a few too.

415
00:14:49,544 --> 00:14:51,711
- Okay, how many do you have?
- 4.

416
00:14:51,711 --> 00:14:54,210
(Run)

417
00:14:57,743 --> 00:15:00,544
(The lonely American)

418
00:15:00,544 --> 00:15:02,347
Whenever I got close,

419
00:15:02,347 --> 00:15:04,377
they all avoided me.

420
00:15:04,377 --> 00:15:06,210
That hurt my feelings.

421
00:15:06,610 --> 00:15:08,456
[JohnnyUS is destined to be lonely]

422
00:15:08,456 --> 00:15:10,876
My youth is just slipping away again.

423
00:15:10,876 --> 00:15:13,444
[Escaping from the predator]

424
00:15:13,444 --> 00:15:14,427
Ji Sung.

425
00:15:14,427 --> 00:15:16,026
["CAMEL"]
I'm pretty sure it's "CAMEL".

426
00:15:16,026 --> 00:15:17,940
[Looks like a gathering of fools]
But I think we need to find a camel now.

427
00:15:17,940 --> 00:15:19,210
I think it's right.

428
00:15:20,063 --> 00:15:22,045
Should I try mimicking a camel?

429
00:15:22,843 --> 00:15:27,110
[The correct answer has 7 letters]
["CAMEL" only has 5 letters]

430
00:15:27,110 --> 00:15:28,559
Oh, it's 7 letters.

431
00:15:28,559 --> 00:15:32,047
Then "Z" could actually be right.

432
00:15:32,047 --> 00:15:34,911
I really can't trust Lee Teuk…

433
00:15:34,911 --> 00:15:36,575
This is driving me crazy.

434
00:15:37,943 --> 00:15:38,744
"Caramel"!!

435
00:15:38,744 --> 00:15:39,976
Oh, never mind.

436
00:15:41,451 --> 00:15:43,717
Sigh… Lee Teuk.

437
00:15:43,717 --> 00:15:46,711
But if we exclude "Z"…

438
00:15:46,711 --> 00:15:47,811
Let's just assume "Z" is correct.

439
00:15:47,811 --> 00:15:49,611
No, I'm gonna ditch the "Z".

440
00:15:49,611 --> 00:15:51,448
The letters spell "CAME…"

441
00:15:51,448 --> 00:15:52,944
Do we fail if we're bad at English?

442
00:15:52,944 --> 00:15:54,339
Yeah, no one's good at English here.

443
00:15:54,339 --> 00:15:57,111
[A natural question pops up]
But Johnny speaks English, so why is he…?

444
00:15:57,111 --> 00:15:58,744
(The lonely American)
This is really hard.

445
00:15:58,744 --> 00:16:00,710
[Holds 3 letters: "M", "A", "C"]

446
00:16:01,522 --> 00:16:03,707
They should've done this in Korean.

447
00:16:03,707 --> 00:16:07,344
Even if we find it, what if
we don't know the English meaning?

448
00:16:07,344 --> 00:16:09,544
[This word is very easy]
There's no way you don't know it.

449
00:16:09,544 --> 00:16:13,617
Only "CARAMEL" comes to mind.
But where is there caramel here?

450
00:16:13,617 --> 00:16:15,385
[Seems like they're almost there]
But it's not "CAMEL", right?

451
00:16:15,385 --> 00:16:17,543
[But still going in circles]
It's not "CAMEL", because there are no camels!

452
00:16:17,543 --> 00:16:21,144
I think a vowel is missing,
since there are 7 letters.

453
00:16:21,144 --> 00:16:22,744
[Shin Dong's Collection Status: A, L, M, R, C, EY]
We can just try adding vowels one by one.

454
00:16:22,744 --> 00:16:24,075
[The last letter still conceals its identity]

455
00:16:24,075 --> 00:16:26,051
I think someone mentioned "U" earlier.

456
00:16:26,943 --> 00:16:28,211
"W".

457
00:16:28,211 --> 00:16:29,844
"U".

458
00:16:29,844 --> 00:16:31,433
"O".

459
00:16:31,433 --> 00:16:32,736
DAWN, how many do you have?

460
00:16:32,736 --> 00:16:35,041
[Tracking the unknown letter here too]
I've got 7 right now, but this…

461
00:16:35,041 --> 00:16:36,205
They said there are 7 letters.

462
00:16:36,205 --> 00:16:39,109
- You saw the bird, right?
- Yeah.

463
00:16:39,109 --> 00:16:40,251
But the birds right now…

464
00:16:40,251 --> 00:16:42,419
[There are 3 types of birds on the decoder]
There's "A" and "M",

465
00:16:42,419 --> 00:16:44,918
and if you look here, there's one more.

466
00:16:44,918 --> 00:16:46,376
Huh?

467
00:16:47,616 --> 00:16:49,343
Huh?

468
00:16:49,343 --> 00:16:51,543
Are there one of each?

469
00:16:51,543 --> 00:16:54,011
I mean... the animals?

470
00:16:54,011 --> 00:16:55,939
There's one of each.

471
00:16:55,939 --> 00:16:57,043
Why?

472
00:16:57,043 --> 00:16:58,844
Then, I think there's a "W".

473
00:16:58,844 --> 00:17:00,244
[The sudden appearance of a "W"]
"W"? Why?

474
00:17:00,244 --> 00:17:02,757
- I think I saw both this and this.
- Oh, really?

475
00:17:02,757 --> 00:17:04,427
I was like,
"These are the same,"

476
00:17:04,427 --> 00:17:07,421
- and I remember skipping it.
- Wait, you saw it somewhere else?

477
00:17:07,421 --> 00:17:08,811
Oh, what? They're the same.

478
00:17:08,811 --> 00:17:12,343
[Skipped because
he had seen this bird before]

479
00:17:12,776 --> 00:17:15,303
[Was the letter he missed "W"?]
Hey, then it must be "W".

480
00:17:15,303 --> 00:17:17,214
- I think it's "W".
- Yo Han, seriously, the two of us…

481
00:17:17,214 --> 00:17:18,347
[A wildcard has appeared]
Let's put our heads together.

482
00:17:18,347 --> 00:17:20,044
Because over there,

483
00:17:20,044 --> 00:17:23,410
there was an eagle somewhere in there.

484
00:17:23,944 --> 00:17:25,444
[The "A" eagle Yo Han mentioned is correct]
Wow! This is bad!

485
00:17:25,444 --> 00:17:27,159
I'm in big trouble!

486
00:17:27,924 --> 00:17:30,044
I saw a similar bird over there again.

487
00:17:30,044 --> 00:17:32,224
So I was like, "What? It's the same,"
and I skipped it.

488
00:17:32,224 --> 00:17:33,944
From what I can see,
it might not be the owl for "M".

489
00:17:33,944 --> 00:17:35,323
You have an "M", right??

490
00:17:35,323 --> 00:17:37,343
There's definitely an owl "M".

491
00:17:37,343 --> 00:17:40,077
[He spotted the owl "M" too]

492
00:17:40,077 --> 00:17:42,543
- I saw the owl for sure.
- Where'd you see the owl?

493
00:17:42,543 --> 00:17:43,853
Where was it again...

494
00:17:43,853 --> 00:17:46,509
- Then did you see three birds?
- Yes.

495
00:17:46,509 --> 00:17:48,877
Then we have 8 letters.

496
00:17:48,877 --> 00:17:52,444
[Chaos ensues with the appearance of "W"]
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8.

497
00:17:52,444 --> 00:17:56,143
[Where did it all go wrong?]
We found a wrong clue somewhere.

498
00:17:56,776 --> 00:18:01,139
[Chapter. 7 God hides His secrets
within the weakest of His creatures]

499
00:18:01,139 --> 00:18:03,428
[Meanwhile, Johnny]
Let's go again!

500
00:18:03,428 --> 00:18:05,275
[Johnny's Collection Status: M, A, C]
Let's start over from the beginning.

501
00:18:07,808 --> 00:18:08,776
Oh!

502
00:18:14,110 --> 00:18:15,811
[Heading out to find the last 3 letters]
"M", "A", "C", "R".

503
00:18:15,811 --> 00:18:19,110
[Johnny's Collection Status: M, A, C, R]

504
00:18:19,110 --> 00:18:21,244
[He searches]
I don't think I checked here yet.

505
00:18:21,244 --> 00:18:22,744
[And searches again]
Oh, it was a nail.

506
00:18:22,744 --> 00:18:25,043
[And searches some more]
Ugh…

507
00:18:26,910 --> 00:18:29,476
[Found a hut beyond the fence]

508
00:18:29,869 --> 00:18:31,911
[This hut is…]

509
00:18:31,911 --> 00:18:33,843
[This is where Yo Han, DAWN, and Lee Teuk…]
Wow! This is bad! I'm in big trouble!

510
00:18:36,544 --> 00:18:39,067
[first found the ancient language early in the mission]
It's here!

511
00:18:39,067 --> 00:18:41,104
It's this!
It's this kind of thing!

512
00:18:46,176 --> 00:18:50,043
[Just like the 3 who came before,]

513
00:18:50,876 --> 00:18:53,976
[Johnny heads inside the fence]

514
00:18:55,527 --> 00:18:57,076
Oh, it's here.

515
00:18:58,443 --> 00:19:00,876
[Found the "A"]

516
00:19:01,376 --> 00:19:03,344
[Johnny's Collection Status: M, A, C, R, A]
Wait, I already had this?

517
00:19:03,344 --> 00:19:04,744
Two "A"s…

518
00:19:04,744 --> 00:19:06,043
Two "A"s…

519
00:19:07,143 --> 00:19:10,343
[There were two "A"s from the start]

520
00:19:11,343 --> 00:19:15,011
[The 7 letters of
the ancients have been revealed]

521
00:19:15,011 --> 00:19:19,176
[When you decode
the 7 letters and combine them]

522
00:19:19,810 --> 00:19:21,877
[Aacelmr]
[Caramel]

523
00:19:21,877 --> 00:19:23,877
[The answer is "CARAMEL"]

524
00:19:23,877 --> 00:19:25,543
[Actually, since earlier,]
Only "CARAMEL" comes to mind.

525
00:19:25,543 --> 00:19:26,342
"Caramel".

526
00:19:26,342 --> 00:19:28,533
[the members have been shouting "CARAMEL"]
Is it "CARAMEL"?

527
00:19:29,236 --> 00:19:31,144
[But the fact that there are two "A"s…]
There should be two "A"s, Lee Teuk.

528
00:19:31,144 --> 00:19:32,943
Then it's not.

529
00:19:32,943 --> 00:19:34,876
Oh, what? They're the same.

530
00:19:34,876 --> 00:19:37,144
[…is something no one realized]

531
00:19:37,144 --> 00:19:41,549
I realized that there are two "A"s.

532
00:19:41,549 --> 00:19:44,011
[The first to realize there are two "A"s]
If this is an "A",

533
00:19:44,011 --> 00:19:46,429
it's either the first
or the second one, right?

534
00:19:46,429 --> 00:19:49,229
[The lonely Chicago guy suddenly rises]
"MAC"… "MAC"…

535
00:19:50,069 --> 00:19:52,650
[Who will find the caramel hidden in this place]
"The one who finds and understands the ancient language"

536
00:19:52,650 --> 00:19:53,839
"will become a prince."

537
00:19:53,839 --> 00:19:55,847
[and bring it to "the highest hut"]
"Blessings await those"

538
00:19:55,847 --> 00:19:58,910
[to become the two princes?]
"who bring 'that' to the highest hut."

539
00:20:03,050 --> 00:20:04,459
Johnny.

540
00:20:04,459 --> 00:20:07,548
- Johnny, can I just team up with you?
- Huh?

541
00:20:07,548 --> 00:20:09,444
Can I just team up with you?

542
00:20:09,444 --> 00:20:10,616
Do you want to?

543
00:20:10,616 --> 00:20:12,654
[After many twists, the NCT alliance is formed]
I got 5 letters.

544
00:20:12,654 --> 00:20:14,521
- How many do you have?
- For now…

545
00:20:14,521 --> 00:20:16,642
[Johnny's Collection Status: M, A, C, R, A]
"E" or "Y".

546
00:20:16,642 --> 00:20:17,836
[Ji Sung's Collection Status: A, L, M, R, C, Z, EY]
What's "E or Y"?

547
00:20:17,836 --> 00:20:18,944
There are both letters.

548
00:20:18,944 --> 00:20:21,244
If you look here, there's "E" and "Y".

549
00:20:21,244 --> 00:20:22,777
Oh, okay. "E".

550
00:20:22,777 --> 00:20:24,644
- "A".
- "A".

551
00:20:24,644 --> 00:20:25,749
[The letters Ji Sung ran around to find]
"L".

552
00:20:25,749 --> 00:20:26,442
[Taking them all]
"L".

553
00:20:26,442 --> 00:20:28,130
- "M".
- "M".

554
00:20:28,130 --> 00:20:29,665
- "R".
- "R".

555
00:20:29,665 --> 00:20:30,944
- "C".
- "C".

556
00:20:30,944 --> 00:20:33,044
- But, I have 2 "A"s.
- What Lee Teuk told me was…

557
00:20:33,044 --> 00:20:34,144
- There are two "A"s?
- Yeah.

558
00:20:34,144 --> 00:20:35,447
[Sharing the most important info]
But that's the owl…

559
00:20:35,447 --> 00:20:37,261
- There are two "A"s?
- Yeah.

560
00:20:37,261 --> 00:20:39,316
Did I see it wrongly?

561
00:20:39,316 --> 00:20:40,464
This is really crucial.

562
00:20:40,464 --> 00:20:41,851
Because the "A" was here.

563
00:20:41,851 --> 00:20:42,851
- The "A" was here?
- Yeah.

564
00:20:42,851 --> 00:20:44,144
Then, there are two "A"s!

565
00:20:44,144 --> 00:20:46,219
- There are two "A"s! There are two!
- Right?

566
00:20:46,219 --> 00:20:48,820
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7.

567
00:20:48,820 --> 00:20:49,758
It's definitely "A".

568
00:20:49,758 --> 00:20:52,195
[Finally, Z is out]
Lee Teuk was really lying!

569
00:20:53,110 --> 00:20:57,876
[Johnny and Ji Sung collected all 7 letters]

570
00:20:57,876 --> 00:21:00,344
[Current letters secured]
[Tied for 1st: Johnny, Ji Sung]

571
00:21:00,344 --> 00:21:03,044
[Tied for 3rd: Shin Dong, DAWN, Yo Han]

572
00:21:03,044 --> 00:21:05,521
[Last place: Lee Teuk]

573
00:21:05,521 --> 00:21:06,328
"Caramely"?

574
00:21:06,328 --> 00:21:08,011
"Caramel"?

575
00:21:08,011 --> 00:21:09,327
[He shouted the answer!]

576
00:21:09,327 --> 00:21:10,535
"A", "A", "C", "R"…

577
00:21:10,535 --> 00:21:13,486
[But no one noticed]
Okay, let's go sit down and figure this out.

578
00:21:13,486 --> 00:21:14,944
[Will they find the answer "CARAMEL"?]
The "A" was right here.

579
00:21:14,944 --> 00:21:16,344
- This was the "A".
- There was an "A" there too.

580
00:21:16,344 --> 00:21:18,044
- Yeah, exactly! Okay, okay!
- There was an "A" there, too.

581
00:21:18,044 --> 00:21:19,577
We found them all.

582
00:21:19,577 --> 00:21:21,950
[DAWN spots the NCT alliance]
How many did you find?

583
00:21:21,950 --> 00:21:23,620
We found all of them just now.

584
00:21:23,620 --> 00:21:24,744
[Ji Sung is giving it away again]
I think we know everything.

585
00:21:24,744 --> 00:21:26,839
The numbers… I mean, we know the spelling.

586
00:21:26,839 --> 00:21:29,052
- But we're can't combine them together right now.
- Really?

587
00:21:29,052 --> 00:21:30,874
[While DAWN and Ji Sung resent Lee Teuk]
Honestly, right now, Lee Teuk…

588
00:21:30,874 --> 00:21:33,876
- Lee Teuk is driving me crazy.
- Oh, I really can't trust Lee Teuk.

589
00:21:33,876 --> 00:21:37,641
[Johnny drifts off alone]
"CARAMELY"? Is there a word like "CARAMELY"?

590
00:21:37,641 --> 00:21:38,975
[Johnny's Collection Status: M, A, C, R, A, EY, L]

591
00:21:38,975 --> 00:21:42,244
I can't trust anyone anymore!
This is no good! I need to go find them myself!

592
00:21:42,244 --> 00:21:45,476
[He just needs to create "CARAMEL"]

593
00:21:48,876 --> 00:21:50,843
[Did he realize it?!]
Oh!

594
00:21:56,310 --> 00:21:58,743
I gotta go to Johnny.

595
00:21:58,743 --> 00:22:00,245
Johnny!

596
00:22:00,245 --> 00:22:02,042
Oh, it's wrong.

597
00:22:02,042 --> 00:22:04,067
- I thought it was "CALAMARI", like squid
- Johnny.

598
00:22:04,067 --> 00:22:06,244
- How many did you find?
- All of them.

599
00:22:06,244 --> 00:22:07,437
- You found them all?
- Yeah.

600
00:22:07,437 --> 00:22:08,931
I have 5.

601
00:22:08,931 --> 00:22:10,543
I can't figure it out.

602
00:22:11,143 --> 00:22:12,726
[On guard]
So?

603
00:22:12,726 --> 00:22:13,841
No, just look at this right now.

604
00:22:13,841 --> 00:22:16,043
[Lee Teuk trying to leech off info]
You're good at English.

605
00:22:16,043 --> 00:22:17,011
So, I'm just curious.

606
00:22:17,011 --> 00:22:18,614
- About what?
- Can you combine these letters?

607
00:22:18,614 --> 00:22:19,552
Not yet.

608
00:22:19,552 --> 00:22:20,544
- It's not, right?
- Yeah.

609
00:22:20,544 --> 00:22:23,511
That means someone lied.

610
00:22:23,511 --> 00:22:25,536
- From what I can tell...
- Yeah?

611
00:22:25,536 --> 00:22:26,644
You lied.

612
00:22:26,644 --> 00:22:27,706
It's not me.

613
00:22:27,706 --> 00:22:29,911
The "Z" you told Ji Sung
about was a lie, right?

614
00:22:29,911 --> 00:22:32,244
That's one I found
by mistake from the start.

615
00:22:32,244 --> 00:22:33,410
Oh, as expected.

616
00:22:33,410 --> 00:22:35,676
No, so basically…

617
00:22:35,676 --> 00:22:37,044
Let's figure it out together.

618
00:22:37,044 --> 00:22:39,843
[Finally gets to the point]
I tried combining them so many times now.

619
00:22:39,843 --> 00:22:41,444
[Glances]
Since you're good at English…

620
00:22:41,444 --> 00:22:42,451
Yeah.

621
00:22:42,451 --> 00:22:43,911
But from what I think…

622
00:22:43,911 --> 00:22:45,244
[Distracting him with conversation]
Yeah?

623
00:22:45,244 --> 00:22:46,257
Yeah.

624
00:22:46,257 --> 00:22:48,144
- But from what I think…
- Yeah?

625
00:22:48,144 --> 00:22:49,077
[Successfully peeked]

626
00:22:49,077 --> 00:22:52,937
Being good at English
doesn't mean you'll get it right.

627
00:22:52,937 --> 00:22:54,256
Oh, really?

628
00:22:54,256 --> 00:22:55,485
(Pretending like he didn't look)
You have the same ones I do!

629
00:22:55,485 --> 00:22:56,436
Take a look!

630
00:22:56,436 --> 00:22:59,611
Why won't you believe me?
These are the ones I got running around at first.

631
00:22:59,611 --> 00:23:01,077
[With his smooth talk,]
It's similar.

632
00:23:01,077 --> 00:23:02,910
[he has Johnny completely fooled]
That's true.

633
00:23:03,443 --> 00:23:04,752
(Sneaking peeks till the very end)

634
00:23:04,752 --> 00:23:06,376
This is the key point.

635
00:23:07,376 --> 00:23:11,043
[Johnny, your notebook has
been completely exposed…]

636
00:23:12,143 --> 00:23:15,010
[Just suffocating]

637
00:23:16,086 --> 00:23:18,143
[CARAMEL]

638
00:23:18,143 --> 00:23:20,710
I got it.

639
00:23:20,710 --> 00:23:24,943
[Johnny figured out "CARAMEL" as the answer]
I got it.

640
00:23:24,943 --> 00:23:26,944
[Following closely]

641
00:23:26,944 --> 00:23:30,443
[Now, he has to find the caramel]

642
00:23:31,776 --> 00:23:34,010
I'm just going my own way.

643
00:23:34,610 --> 00:23:35,944
[Desperate]
Let's do it together.

644
00:23:35,944 --> 00:23:37,626
Please, Johnny.

645
00:23:37,626 --> 00:23:39,043
Let's team up.

646
00:23:39,043 --> 00:23:41,288
[So, where can he find the caramel?]
But I have no idea where I'm supposed to find it.

647
00:23:41,288 --> 00:23:43,365
Exactly, tell me so I can help you.

648
00:23:44,644 --> 00:23:45,813
This feels so refreshing.

649
00:23:45,813 --> 00:23:47,744
- You know what it is?
- Yeah.

650
00:23:47,744 --> 00:23:49,306
Let's share it.

651
00:23:49,306 --> 00:23:50,838
[The hyenas surround Johnny]
Oh, guys. But what are you gonna do?

652
00:23:50,838 --> 00:23:52,111
You should've been quiet about this!

653
00:23:52,111 --> 00:23:54,343
I'm the only one who knows right now.

654
00:23:54,343 --> 00:23:57,010
(Just tell me)
What are you gonna do?

655
00:24:00,543 --> 00:24:01,844
If that's the case,
don't tell anyone else.

656
00:24:01,844 --> 00:24:04,134
- Don't share with anyone.
- Yeah, I won't.

657
00:24:04,134 --> 00:24:06,429
Let's share it! Wait, come over here.

658
00:24:06,429 --> 00:24:08,344
Oh, wait! Come here for a second.

659
00:24:08,344 --> 00:24:11,661
[Lee Teuk feels frustrated not knowing the answer]
Oh, this seriously feels so refreshing right now.

660
00:24:11,661 --> 00:24:14,085
- What?
- Let's find it together.

661
00:24:17,276 --> 00:24:19,244
It's 7 letters.

662
00:24:19,244 --> 00:24:22,043
[So what's the combo?]
I know it's 7 letters.

663
00:24:22,043 --> 00:24:24,044
I should've been born in the US too.

664
00:24:24,044 --> 00:24:25,731
- But…
- Yeah?

665
00:24:25,731 --> 00:24:27,854
[Shin Dong approaches again]
I'll tell you, Lee Teuk…

666
00:24:27,854 --> 00:24:30,080
- No, no, no. Let me tell you.
- Yeah.

667
00:24:30,080 --> 00:24:32,644
- Is it "CARAMEL" or not?
- Oh, really?

668
00:24:32,644 --> 00:24:35,776
[Shin Dong figured out the answer too]
Is it or is it not? From what you know.

669
00:24:36,386 --> 00:24:37,387
[Now Shin Dong and Johnny
are the ones who know the answer]

670
00:24:37,387 --> 00:24:39,112
- Yeah.
- Yeah, okay.

671
00:24:40,116 --> 00:24:42,157
- What? Do you two know?
- Did you figure it out?

672
00:24:42,157 --> 00:24:44,423
- So where is that exactly?
- Hey!

673
00:24:44,423 --> 00:24:46,361
- Let me in on it too!
- I have no clue.

674
00:24:46,361 --> 00:24:47,828
- How'd you find it?
- I have no idea, Lee Teuk.

675
00:24:47,828 --> 00:24:50,476
- How'd you combine it?
- I said I don't know.

676
00:24:50,476 --> 00:24:52,476
[Pouting]

677
00:24:52,868 --> 00:24:54,237
[On the move to find caramel]
Have you gone this way, Shin Dong?

678
00:24:54,237 --> 00:24:56,506
But there are no cameras over here.

679
00:24:56,506 --> 00:24:58,238
But the cameras are following us…

680
00:24:58,238 --> 00:25:01,110
[They head to the minibar…]

681
00:25:02,976 --> 00:25:04,046
[Looks like a dead end]

682
00:25:04,046 --> 00:25:05,939
I don't think it's this way.

683
00:25:05,939 --> 00:25:07,349
[Lee Teuk, who was following, also stops]

684
00:25:07,349 --> 00:25:08,910
Where is it exactly?

685
00:25:08,910 --> 00:25:12,410
(Pretending to combine the letters)

686
00:25:16,143 --> 00:25:19,094
[Just then, his NCT ally passes by]

687
00:25:19,094 --> 00:25:20,228
Ji Sung.

688
00:25:20,228 --> 00:25:21,430
[Everyone reacts]
Yes?

689
00:25:21,430 --> 00:25:22,948
Did you find it?

690
00:25:22,948 --> 00:25:25,610
(Come here)
Did you find it?

691
00:25:25,610 --> 00:25:29,410
[Following closely]

692
00:25:30,043 --> 00:25:32,176
[Spotted the crew tagging along]

693
00:25:33,710 --> 00:25:35,110
Johnny!

694
00:25:36,476 --> 00:25:39,343
I'll help you find it!
I'm good at finding stuff.

695
00:25:39,343 --> 00:25:40,944
Did you find it?

696
00:25:40,944 --> 00:25:42,144
I figured it out.

697
00:25:42,144 --> 00:25:43,244
- Really?!
- Yeah.

698
00:25:43,244 --> 00:25:44,046
- What is it?
- Why? Why? Why?

699
00:25:44,046 --> 00:25:47,044
[Ji Sung shared a lot with Johnny]
But I shared everything with him.

700
00:25:47,044 --> 00:25:48,046
So, I'll tell you, Ji Sung.

701
00:25:48,046 --> 00:25:49,244
- You can't do that.
- Why not?

702
00:25:49,244 --> 00:25:50,267
[Unreasonable]
Ji Sung doesn't know either.

703
00:25:50,267 --> 00:25:51,958
Oh, he told me the number.

704
00:25:51,958 --> 00:25:54,343
We need to have an NCT meeting.

705
00:25:55,876 --> 00:25:58,200
It's "CARAMEL".

706
00:25:58,200 --> 00:25:59,043
Got it?

707
00:25:59,043 --> 00:26:00,363
- Is it really that?
- Yeah.

708
00:26:00,363 --> 00:26:02,075
[Find it quickly, Ji Sung]
But Shin Dong knows it too.

709
00:26:03,243 --> 00:26:05,626
That's actually what
we did in the beginning!

710
00:26:05,626 --> 00:26:08,454
We need to find the caramel.

711
00:26:08,454 --> 00:26:09,892
Yeah, but how do we find it?

712
00:26:11,076 --> 00:26:12,276
[Hop]

713
00:26:14,544 --> 00:26:17,244
Excuse me, sir.

714
00:26:17,244 --> 00:26:18,706
By any chance…

715
00:26:19,810 --> 00:26:21,544
Do you… Do you have "CARAMEL"?

716
00:26:21,544 --> 00:26:22,993
- Caramel?
- Yes.

717
00:26:22,993 --> 00:26:24,628
[Lee Teuk trails closely again]

718
00:26:24,628 --> 00:26:27,045
Do you… Do you have "CARAMEL"?

719
00:26:27,045 --> 00:26:28,531
- Caramel?
- Yeah.

720
00:26:28,531 --> 00:26:30,343
Caramel, caramel.

721
00:26:30,343 --> 00:26:32,710
[He heard "CARAMEL"!]

722
00:26:33,343 --> 00:26:38,510
["CARAMEL" reaches Lee Teuk's ears]

723
00:26:40,010 --> 00:26:42,511
[4 people know the answer]

724
00:26:42,511 --> 00:26:46,077
[But there are only two spots]
The prince status will be given to only two people.

725
00:26:46,077 --> 00:26:50,167
[No one knows where the caramel is]

726
00:26:50,167 --> 00:26:51,244
Please say it's correct.

727
00:26:51,244 --> 00:26:52,444
Oh, but I think it's right.

728
00:26:52,444 --> 00:26:53,524
He's caught on, he's caught on!

729
00:26:53,524 --> 00:26:54,991
[Who will get to be the prince?!]

730
00:26:54,991 --> 00:26:56,690
Where could it be?

731
00:26:59,343 --> 00:27:03,010
By any chance, do you have caramel?

732
00:27:04,510 --> 00:27:07,643
[Candidate Johnny visits the restaurant]

733
00:27:07,643 --> 00:27:10,811
[Cautious]
Do you have "CARAMEL"?

734
00:27:10,811 --> 00:27:11,644
[No idea]

735
00:27:11,644 --> 00:27:13,739
No? No caramel? No?

736
00:27:13,739 --> 00:27:17,444
[Candidate Shin Dong does a staff body check]
Director, got anything in your pockets?

737
00:27:17,444 --> 00:27:19,844
[Is he a troublemaker or what…?]
Do you have it or not?

738
00:27:19,844 --> 00:27:21,673
Director, you don't have anything?

739
00:27:25,843 --> 00:27:30,076
[Shin Dong trudges along]
It's gotta be here somewhere.

740
00:27:37,110 --> 00:27:40,076
[and even checks inside the accommodation]

741
00:27:40,576 --> 00:27:42,444
What's crazy about my gut feeling is…

742
00:27:42,444 --> 00:27:46,911
I just wanted to try opening up
the window at our accommodation.

743
00:27:46,911 --> 00:27:49,344
[Something came to mind as he opened the door]
When I got close and tried opening it, it opened.

744
00:27:49,344 --> 00:27:51,577
Then something flashed through my mind.

745
00:27:51,577 --> 00:27:54,244
When we first went upstairs
to check the rooms,

746
00:27:54,244 --> 00:27:56,177
I remembered there was
a mounted camera by the stairs.

747
00:27:56,177 --> 00:27:57,977
If that's still recording,

748
00:27:57,977 --> 00:28:00,776
the answer's gotta be
in the accommodation.

749
00:28:02,876 --> 00:28:04,211
[Checking the camera]

750
00:28:04,211 --> 00:28:06,843
Oh? It's still rolling!

751
00:28:07,412 --> 00:28:08,843
Oh? It's still rolling!

752
00:28:10,110 --> 00:28:12,943
[Will Shin Dong's gut feeling turn out right?]

753
00:28:18,276 --> 00:28:21,410
[Found the caramel]

754
00:28:22,543 --> 00:28:26,910
[Caramel found, thanks to
this entertainer's gut feeling]

755
00:28:28,610 --> 00:28:31,143
[Sprinting]
[Setting a new personal record for speed]

756
00:28:31,621 --> 00:28:33,390
[He brings the "CARAMEL" to the "highest hut"]

757
00:28:33,390 --> 00:28:34,625
Did you find it?

758
00:28:34,625 --> 00:28:36,247
I was searching for ages
to find where it was!

759
00:28:36,247 --> 00:28:37,621
Please give it to me.

760
00:28:38,360 --> 00:28:39,376
Caramel.

761
00:28:39,376 --> 00:28:42,469
Shin Dong, you are today's first prince.

762
00:28:42,469 --> 00:28:45,802
[Shin Dong confirmed as a prince]
I'm the prince!

763
00:28:46,970 --> 00:28:49,244
I got the answer
using the letters Ji Sung gave me,

764
00:28:49,244 --> 00:28:51,977
and I found it after
Johnny gave me confirmation.

765
00:28:51,977 --> 00:28:54,843
I've never seen the "ancient language".

766
00:28:54,843 --> 00:28:56,546
I never cross-checked it, not even once.

767
00:28:56,546 --> 00:28:59,863
Yet, I became the first prince.

768
00:28:59,863 --> 00:29:03,063
- I'm the prince!
- Oh, come on!

769
00:29:04,487 --> 00:29:07,010
Why is Shin Dong so good at games?

770
00:29:07,010 --> 00:29:09,076
I'm the prince!

771
00:29:14,829 --> 00:29:15,847
Seriously?

772
00:29:15,847 --> 00:29:19,102
Where is it... Shin Dong,
where did you get it from?

773
00:29:19,102 --> 00:29:22,902
[Arrived at the restaurant Johnny checked earlier]
Is it not here? Doesn't it feel like it should?

774
00:29:23,343 --> 00:29:24,943
Excuse me!

775
00:29:24,943 --> 00:29:26,657
Do you have caramel?

776
00:29:26,657 --> 00:29:28,743
[No idea]
No?

777
00:29:29,710 --> 00:29:32,310
[The struggle to find caramel]

778
00:29:33,239 --> 00:29:34,454
Only one spot, only one spot.

779
00:29:34,454 --> 00:29:37,143
I really don't want
to play the next game!

780
00:29:37,954 --> 00:29:40,096
[Spotted caramel syrup at the bar]

781
00:29:40,096 --> 00:29:41,796
This… uh…

782
00:29:42,626 --> 00:29:44,242
(Please)
Sir.

783
00:29:44,242 --> 00:29:45,744
Just one minute, just one minute

784
00:29:45,744 --> 00:29:47,164
- We can't.
- Really?

785
00:29:48,076 --> 00:29:50,476
[Desperate plan fails]
30… 30 seconds!

786
00:29:50,476 --> 00:29:52,711
I run fast! Oh my god!

787
00:29:52,711 --> 00:29:54,537
Trururururu!

788
00:29:54,537 --> 00:29:57,687
[Please]
Please, please!

789
00:29:57,687 --> 00:29:59,348
[How much will it take?]
How much?

790
00:29:59,348 --> 00:30:01,376
Oh, what do I do…?

791
00:30:01,376 --> 00:30:05,677
Shin Dong! Can you just tell me
the first letter? Shin Dong!

792
00:30:05,677 --> 00:30:08,583
I'll tell you what it's not. Call it out!

793
00:30:08,583 --> 00:30:11,821
"E", "A", "L",

794
00:30:11,821 --> 00:30:14,555
"M", "R", "Z"…

795
00:30:14,555 --> 00:30:15,909
Definitely not "Z".

796
00:30:15,909 --> 00:30:17,152
[Now, everyone knows about the fake "Z"]
You guys got totally played by the "Z".

797
00:30:17,152 --> 00:30:19,354
- The "Z" was Lee Teuk's decoy.
- Ugh! Lee Teuk! Lee Teuk!

798
00:30:19,354 --> 00:30:20,810
- Lee Teuk was lying.
- It's a lie, huh?

799
00:30:20,810 --> 00:30:22,310
I'm telling you it's right!

800
00:30:22,310 --> 00:30:23,977
Yo Han, hurry up...

801
00:30:23,977 --> 00:30:26,636
No, it's every man for himself now.

802
00:30:26,636 --> 00:30:28,972
It's every man for himself now.

803
00:30:28,972 --> 00:30:32,640
[Who will be the last prince?!]
I just need to find it.

804
00:30:32,640 --> 00:30:33,677
I think I got it.

805
00:30:35,643 --> 00:30:37,137
[Just then, Lee Teuk comes running]

806
00:30:37,137 --> 00:30:38,915
I'm…!

807
00:30:38,915 --> 00:30:41,382
[Johnny sprints too!]
I'm…!

808
00:30:42,243 --> 00:30:44,944
[Johnny arrives first]
I'm…!

809
00:30:44,944 --> 00:30:46,342
Oh, what?

810
00:30:46,342 --> 00:30:47,744
[Will the game end just like this?]
I guess it's over.

811
00:30:47,744 --> 00:30:49,037
It's over.

812
00:30:49,037 --> 00:30:51,732
I just wanna see if it's right… Is it right?

813
00:30:51,732 --> 00:30:54,111
No… This is a lie.

814
00:30:54,111 --> 00:30:55,244
Johnny.

815
00:30:55,244 --> 00:30:56,944
You are the second prince!

816
00:30:56,944 --> 00:30:58,344
I'm…!

817
00:30:58,344 --> 00:31:01,943
[Johnny confirmed as prince]
The prince!

818
00:31:01,943 --> 00:31:03,876
Yeah!!!

819
00:31:03,876 --> 00:31:05,611
[3 minutes ago]

820
00:31:05,611 --> 00:31:08,176
I haven't checked this place yet.

821
00:31:09,076 --> 00:31:10,832
[Start searching the unchecked
prince's accommodation]

822
00:31:10,832 --> 00:31:14,144
Before going up to the restaurant,
I asked the staff.

823
00:31:14,144 --> 00:31:16,811
"Can we go anywhere? Even the restaurant?"

824
00:31:16,811 --> 00:31:20,790
They said "Yes," and that's when I knew.

825
00:31:20,790 --> 00:31:24,643
Then I need to check this place,
and that place as well.

826
00:31:27,010 --> 00:31:29,044
I'm really bad at treasure hunts.

827
00:31:29,044 --> 00:31:30,144
That's really a fact.

828
00:31:30,144 --> 00:31:33,503
This is the first time
in my life I've won one.

829
00:31:33,503 --> 00:31:36,877
I'm not usually
the type to shout like that.

830
00:31:36,877 --> 00:31:39,844
- I guess I can shout too.
- I'm the prince!

831
00:31:39,844 --> 00:31:41,531
It felt amazing.

832
00:31:41,531 --> 00:31:43,133
Yeah!!

833
00:31:43,133 --> 00:31:44,244
Hey, where did you find it?

834
00:31:44,244 --> 00:31:46,010
- Wow!
- Hey, where did you find it?

835
00:31:46,010 --> 00:31:49,643
I'm the prince!

836
00:31:53,376 --> 00:31:56,410
[Walking toward the shout of the prince,]

837
00:31:57,676 --> 00:32:00,610
[Ji Sung falls to his knees]

838
00:32:02,018 --> 00:32:03,710
[Honestly, Ji Sung...]

839
00:32:04,210 --> 00:32:04,977
"Caramel".

840
00:32:04,977 --> 00:32:06,166
[He said the answer
just 10 minutes into the mission]

841
00:32:06,166 --> 00:32:07,831
Oh, "CARAMEL"?

842
00:32:07,831 --> 00:32:09,432
[He kept saying "CARAMEL" many times after that]
Is it "CARAMEL"?

843
00:32:09,432 --> 00:32:10,611
"Caramel". "Caramel"?

844
00:32:10,611 --> 00:32:11,944
"Caramel"? "Caramel".

845
00:32:11,944 --> 00:32:13,811
What worries me is
if the answer's already been revealed

846
00:32:13,811 --> 00:32:16,711
and I don't know what it is,
it'd be kind of embarrassing.

847
00:32:16,711 --> 00:32:17,917
[Embarrassed Ji Sung,]
Today, I really have to…

848
00:32:17,917 --> 00:32:19,144
[who really wanted to be a prince]
I really have to become a prince.

849
00:32:19,144 --> 00:32:20,977
I really want to be a prince.

850
00:32:20,977 --> 00:32:22,144
- Ugh.
- Wow!

851
00:32:22,144 --> 00:32:24,276
[1st Pauper status]

852
00:32:24,929 --> 00:32:27,044
Whether it made me look good or bad,

853
00:32:27,044 --> 00:32:30,444
[Even set aside his image]
I was so determined to become a prince.

854
00:32:30,444 --> 00:32:34,264
[What he got back was his 2nd Pauper status]
Ugh, this is so unfair!

855
00:32:34,264 --> 00:32:36,943
[The world's first double pauper]
The world's first to be a pauper twice in a row.

856
00:32:36,943 --> 00:32:39,969
[After getting his 3rd Pauper status in a row]
A woodpecker on the left, and a club on the right.

857
00:32:39,969 --> 00:32:41,844
[He achieved his 4th Pauper status]

858
00:32:41,844 --> 00:32:45,577
[Basically ALL Pauper status]
I'm actually achieving this epic feat.

859
00:32:45,577 --> 00:32:47,644
I didn't choose to be a pauper
because I wanted to be one.

860
00:32:47,644 --> 00:32:49,833
I worked so hard, but ended up a pauper.

861
00:32:50,937 --> 00:32:54,576
I couldn't believe it for like 5, 10 minutes.

862
00:32:55,643 --> 00:32:59,369
[Lee Teuk confirmed as a pauper]
I'm…! I'm the pauper!

863
00:32:59,369 --> 00:33:02,025
I thought I had it,
but when it didn't happen,

864
00:33:02,025 --> 00:33:04,729
it just stopped being fun.

865
00:33:04,729 --> 00:33:07,261
All the princes have been decided.

866
00:33:07,643 --> 00:33:10,810
DAWN! You're a pauper!

867
00:33:11,276 --> 00:33:13,544
Yo Han's the physical member, right?

868
00:33:13,544 --> 00:33:17,544
I thought about coaxing Yo Han
and taking his letters.

869
00:33:17,544 --> 00:33:20,477
[Picked the wrong target]
But Yo Han gave me wrong information too.

870
00:33:20,477 --> 00:33:24,044
The main reason I lost was that I misread him.

871
00:33:24,044 --> 00:33:25,844
- DAWN, you're a pauper!
- No, no!

872
00:33:25,844 --> 00:33:27,744
Why aren't you saying it
to Yo Han and only to me?

873
00:33:27,744 --> 00:33:29,877
Yo Han, you are a pauper too.

874
00:33:29,877 --> 00:33:31,103
What the heck.

875
00:33:31,103 --> 00:33:32,224
[Shin Dong: Prince 3, Pauper 1]
[Johnny: Prince 2, Pauper 2]

876
00:33:32,224 --> 00:33:33,444
[DAWN: Prince 3, Pauper 1]
[Yo Han: Prince 1, Pauper 3]

877
00:33:33,444 --> 00:33:34,745
[Lee Teuk: Prince 2, Pauper 2]
[Ji Sung: Prince 0, Pauper 4]

878
00:33:34,745 --> 00:33:35,653
[Disappointed]
It's all over.

879
00:33:35,653 --> 00:33:37,011
Oh, but I really could've done that…!

880
00:33:37,011 --> 00:33:40,644
I thought there was something
if I finished drinking the mango juice.

881
00:33:40,644 --> 00:33:41,529
[Gave himself an extra mission]
So you drank it all?

882
00:33:41,529 --> 00:33:42,844
I drank all of this!

883
00:33:42,844 --> 00:33:45,829
Yo Han, you should've
teamed up with me.

884
00:33:45,829 --> 00:33:49,228
I thought the mission
was to finish the mango juice.

885
00:33:49,228 --> 00:33:51,736
[A fitting remark for someone who lost]
That's why I drank all the mango juice!

886
00:33:51,736 --> 00:33:53,849
- Was that left for us to drink?
- Yes.

887
00:33:53,849 --> 00:33:55,844
But you don't know
how long that juice was out there.

888
00:33:55,844 --> 00:33:59,117
We left it for you
to drink in case you got tired.

889
00:33:59,117 --> 00:34:00,717
- Oh!
- Oh, really?

890
00:34:00,717 --> 00:34:03,373
No wonder it kept appearing.
I almost drank them all.

891
00:34:03,373 --> 00:34:04,452
The correct answer was this.

892
00:34:04,452 --> 00:34:06,651
[The caramel they had been searching for]
Where was this?

893
00:34:06,651 --> 00:34:07,611
- In the room.
- It was in the room.

894
00:34:07,611 --> 00:34:09,944
[Bummer]
Room 1 and Room 4 had them.

895
00:34:09,944 --> 00:34:11,744
- Here, take one each.
- I'm not eating it.

896
00:34:11,744 --> 00:34:13,843
I don't want to eat it.

897
00:34:13,843 --> 00:34:15,544
(Into my mouth then)

898
00:34:15,544 --> 00:34:18,052
Today's princes are Shin Dong and Johnny.

899
00:34:18,052 --> 00:34:19,643
[Shin Dong and Johnny
confirmed as the 4th princes]

900
00:34:22,110 --> 00:34:25,177
[Shin Dong, Johnny, the 4th princes are born]

901
00:34:25,177 --> 00:34:27,639
[Without finding a single clue,]
It looked like Shin Dong didn't do any legwork,

902
00:34:27,639 --> 00:34:28,571
[Shin Dong became a prince]
but found it anyway.

903
00:34:28,571 --> 00:34:30,437
That's the wisdom of life.

904
00:34:30,437 --> 00:34:32,233
I told him too much!

905
00:34:32,233 --> 00:34:34,011
But Ji Sung is really kind,

906
00:34:34,011 --> 00:34:36,951
[Ji Sung gives generously]
because he told us everything!

907
00:34:36,951 --> 00:34:38,848
I was like, "Ji Sung, let's share."

908
00:34:38,848 --> 00:34:40,644
He told me all of his letters
and then ran off!

909
00:34:40,644 --> 00:34:42,210
- What?
- Huh??

910
00:34:42,210 --> 00:34:44,244
- Right, director? Right?
- Hey, what?

911
00:34:44,244 --> 00:34:45,593
- You're an angel!
- When… When was that?

912
00:34:45,593 --> 00:34:47,163
Hey, did you not need mine?

913
00:34:47,163 --> 00:34:49,132
- When I saw you in the beginning…
- No, it's not that…

914
00:34:49,132 --> 00:34:50,843
I don't really remember this, but…

915
00:34:50,843 --> 00:34:52,344
I was really busy.

916
00:34:52,344 --> 00:34:54,777
I was so focused on finding it no matter what,
so I was really busy.

917
00:34:54,777 --> 00:34:56,812
And so,

918
00:34:56,812 --> 00:34:58,321
[DAWN's first time being a pauper]
our DAWN's streak

919
00:34:58,321 --> 00:35:00,643
- of being a prince is broken.
- Oh, finally!

920
00:35:00,643 --> 00:35:01,963
- But…!
- Ji Sung…

921
00:35:01,963 --> 00:35:05,347
[Ji Sung achieves ALL Pauper status]
Ji Sung's streak of being a pauper continues!

922
00:35:05,347 --> 00:35:06,759
Wow, this is amazing.

923
00:35:06,759 --> 00:35:08,240
Pauper, pauper, pauper, pauper.

924
00:35:08,240 --> 00:35:10,340
- Ji Sung's energy is on another level.
- This game was hard.

925
00:35:10,340 --> 00:35:13,450
[Pauper Ji Sung, Season 2 confirmed]
Ji Sung's locked in for Season 2.

926
00:35:13,450 --> 00:35:15,766
Will Ji Sung stay a pauper again in Season 2?

927
00:35:15,766 --> 00:35:17,645
- Alright, good job, everyone.
- Yes.

928
00:35:17,645 --> 00:35:19,093
- In a bit…
- I was so close…!

929
00:35:19,093 --> 00:35:21,844
we will begin the prince's pool party,
attended by the paupers.

930
00:35:21,844 --> 00:35:23,663
- Wow, that's awesome!
- Then, what do we do?

931
00:35:23,663 --> 00:35:25,602
Attended… We're attending to them?

932
00:35:25,602 --> 00:35:29,036
- Then you gotta wait outside with towels.
- Yes, like bring towels and drinks.

933
00:35:29,036 --> 00:35:31,458
[His first pauper run is a tough one]
Wow, nice.

934
00:35:31,458 --> 00:35:33,144
[With the paupers attending to them,]
This is nice, being a prince on the last day!

935
00:35:33,144 --> 00:35:35,310
[the princes' pool party begins]
Ji Sung, let's look forward to Season 2.

936
00:35:36,242 --> 00:35:38,377
- Your Highnesses, you must be tired.
- Yes.

937
00:35:38,377 --> 00:35:41,010
Instead of swimming,
how about going in and resting?

938
00:35:43,449 --> 00:35:45,755
[Ignoring]
This is so nice.

939
00:35:45,755 --> 00:35:49,244
[The princes casually take a seat]
Oh, princes, please have a seat.

940
00:35:49,244 --> 00:35:51,660
Our paupers…!
Oh, you're all dressed nicely today.

941
00:35:51,660 --> 00:35:52,857
[Flattery Mode ON]
Oh, our prince!

942
00:35:52,857 --> 00:35:54,411
This is nice. I love this kind of thing.

943
00:35:54,411 --> 00:35:55,279
Prince!

944
00:35:55,279 --> 00:35:56,429
[Satisfied]
I'm into things like this.

945
00:35:56,429 --> 00:35:58,049
- Oh, you're really tense!
- Yeah.

946
00:35:58,049 --> 00:35:59,277
You're really tense here.

947
00:35:59,277 --> 00:36:00,459
[Human fan ON]

948
00:36:00,459 --> 00:36:02,366
- Oh my.
- This is so nice.

949
00:36:02,366 --> 00:36:04,160
Alright, first things first!

950
00:36:04,160 --> 00:36:06,177
When you come to
a place like this for vacation,

951
00:36:06,177 --> 00:36:07,721
resting is all well and nice,

952
00:36:07,721 --> 00:36:09,649
but I'm craving something refreshing.

953
00:36:09,649 --> 00:36:11,344
Something refreshing! Watermelon juice!

954
00:36:11,344 --> 00:36:13,351
The four of you play Rock-Paper-Scissors.

955
00:36:13,351 --> 00:36:15,011
- Play Rock-Paper-Scissors…
- Rock-Paper-Scissors?

956
00:36:15,011 --> 00:36:16,336
And the one who loses!

957
00:36:16,336 --> 00:36:18,210
- Just one person?
- Yes, just one person

958
00:36:18,210 --> 00:36:20,211
[Bring the drinks]
will go and grab the drinks.

959
00:36:20,211 --> 00:36:22,144
[Whining]
You should've said something sooner...

960
00:36:22,144 --> 00:36:23,124
I just thought of it.

961
00:36:23,124 --> 00:36:24,659
- Oh, you just thought of it now?
- Yeah, it just came to me.

962
00:36:24,659 --> 00:36:26,176
- Yeah, it's a bit far.
- Alright.

963
00:36:26,176 --> 00:36:28,744
Being a prince means having power.

964
00:36:28,744 --> 00:36:30,277
[Ready to enjoy it fully]
I gotta use it a lot at times like this.

965
00:36:30,277 --> 00:36:35,010
[Pure joy]
Honestly, it was pure bliss for us.

966
00:36:35,636 --> 00:36:37,949
- And everyone.
- Yes?

967
00:36:37,949 --> 00:36:41,543
I thought telling you this early on
would make you work harder.

968
00:36:41,543 --> 00:36:44,544
We'll pick the best pauper.

969
00:36:44,544 --> 00:36:45,744
We've prepared a big gift!

970
00:36:45,744 --> 00:36:47,019
[Intrigued]
What is it? What?

971
00:36:47,019 --> 00:36:48,116
[Best Pauper Awards]
Could it be a room?

972
00:36:48,116 --> 00:36:49,531
You're giving us a room?

973
00:36:49,531 --> 00:36:51,528
[What's the perk of being the Best Pauper?]
It's a surprise gift, everyone.

974
00:36:51,528 --> 00:36:53,734
- So, you gotta work hard, okay?
- Oh, tell us what it is! I'm curious!

975
00:36:53,734 --> 00:36:55,035
[What on earth is it?]
Can't you tell us?

976
00:36:55,035 --> 00:36:56,486
Are we moving up in status?

977
00:36:56,486 --> 00:36:59,343
[To be revealed shortly]
After we've checked, I'll tell you.

978
00:36:59,343 --> 00:37:00,610
Okay, okay.

979
00:37:00,610 --> 00:37:03,965
[Resuming the drink errand bet]
The loser of Rock-Paper-Scissors.

980
00:37:03,965 --> 00:37:04,966
Is the loser going?

981
00:37:04,966 --> 00:37:05,968
- The loser.
- Yes.

982
00:37:05,968 --> 00:37:07,844
If you just want to go, you can.

983
00:37:07,844 --> 00:37:09,237
[Lee Teuk and Yo Han will go]
I'll go and come back!

984
00:37:09,237 --> 00:37:11,044
- I'll go!
- Anyone who wants to go can go.

985
00:37:11,044 --> 00:37:12,444
[Are we really going?]

986
00:37:12,444 --> 00:37:13,264
We'll just play Rock-Paper-Scissors!

987
00:37:13,264 --> 00:37:15,412
Since it's the first one and all.

988
00:37:15,412 --> 00:37:17,713
- I love your enthusiasm!
- Yes, alright.

989
00:37:17,713 --> 00:37:18,746
Okay, everyone.

990
00:37:18,746 --> 00:37:20,744
- It's too obvious for the loser to go, so…
- The 1st-place winner?

991
00:37:20,744 --> 00:37:22,711
[The 2nd-place winner will go]
2nd place will go!

992
00:37:22,711 --> 00:37:25,018
- The 2nd-place winner will go.
- I like things like this.

993
00:37:25,018 --> 00:37:26,710
So, 2nd place will go.

994
00:37:26,710 --> 00:37:28,444
Shoot or 1st place!

995
00:37:28,444 --> 00:37:30,155
[Scissors / Rock / Scissors / Paper]
Rock-Paper-Scissors!

996
00:37:30,155 --> 00:37:31,448
[Rock / Scissors / Paper / Scissors]
Rock-Paper-Scissors!

997
00:37:31,448 --> 00:37:33,697
[Paper / Paper / Rock / Paper]
Rock-Paper-Scissors!

998
00:37:33,697 --> 00:37:36,499
[Last place Ji Sung is excluded]
Okay, last place, step out!

999
00:37:36,499 --> 00:37:38,902
[The 2nd-place winner among the three goes]
So, 2nd place among you three.

1000
00:37:38,902 --> 00:37:40,344
Shoot or 3rd place!

1001
00:37:40,344 --> 00:37:42,144
[Scissors / Rock / Scissors]
Rock-Paper-Scissors!

1002
00:37:42,144 --> 00:37:43,140
- Okay!
- Oh!

1003
00:37:43,140 --> 00:37:45,762
[DAWN excluded]
The winner between you two will go.

1004
00:37:45,762 --> 00:37:48,143
- Lee Teuk, it's because we said we'd go!
- We said we'd go…!

1005
00:37:48,143 --> 00:37:49,536
Shoot or win!

1006
00:37:49,536 --> 00:37:51,577
[Rock / Scissors]
Rock-Paper-Scissors!

1007
00:37:51,577 --> 00:37:52,840
[Yo Han wins]
Sweet!

1008
00:37:52,840 --> 00:37:55,254
- Off you go!
- Oh, nice, nice!

1009
00:37:55,254 --> 00:37:57,162
Nice! Oh, what do you want?

1010
00:37:57,162 --> 00:37:59,439
[I'll take your orders, Your Highnesses]
An iced Americano with extra ice.

1011
00:37:59,439 --> 00:38:01,744
And a Coke Zero with ice.

1012
00:38:01,744 --> 00:38:04,210
Pauper! Can you get us some too?

1013
00:38:05,128 --> 00:38:06,620
[Okay, got it]
Okay! I'm feeling generous! What do you want?

1014
00:38:06,620 --> 00:38:08,077
- I'll have a Coke.
- A Coke.

1015
00:38:08,077 --> 00:38:09,444
- Zero!
- A Coke Zero.

1016
00:38:09,444 --> 00:38:10,644
- I want a Coke too!
- A Coke.

1017
00:38:10,644 --> 00:38:13,347
Two regular Cokes,
Two Coke Zeros, an Iced Americano.

1018
00:38:13,347 --> 00:38:14,862
- One with lots of ice, please.
- Oh, I'll take a Coke Zero too.

1019
00:38:14,862 --> 00:38:16,943
[Orders start flooding in]
Three Coke Zeros…

1020
00:38:16,943 --> 00:38:18,711
- A regular Coke.
- One regular Coke.

1021
00:38:18,711 --> 00:38:20,735
- Ice, ice!
- Ice…

1022
00:38:20,735 --> 00:38:22,440
Why are you being like this, Lee Teuk?

1023
00:38:22,440 --> 00:38:24,416
[We were gonna go together earlier…]
Lee Teuk, we were supposed to do it together.

1024
00:38:24,416 --> 00:38:26,581
- Is it heavy?
- Yeah, carrying five is kinda tough.

1025
00:38:26,581 --> 00:38:28,044
- Oh, really? Shall we go together?
- Let's go together then.

1026
00:38:28,044 --> 00:38:29,643
Go on ahead.

1027
00:38:29,643 --> 00:38:31,144
Do you want one more person?

1028
00:38:31,144 --> 00:38:34,222
Because I might drop something on the way.

1029
00:38:34,222 --> 00:38:35,674
I have to carry them
with both hands like this.

1030
00:38:35,674 --> 00:38:36,811
[Alright, send one more pauper!]
Okay, the three of you

1031
00:38:36,811 --> 00:38:37,855
will play Rock-Paper-Scissors again.

1032
00:38:37,855 --> 00:38:38,702
Who's going?

1033
00:38:38,702 --> 00:38:40,372
[The 2nd-place winner again]
2nd place will go. 2nd place!

1034
00:38:40,372 --> 00:38:41,529
- Rock-Paper-Scissors!
- Rock-Paper-Scissors!

1035
00:38:41,529 --> 00:38:43,044
[Rock / Paper / Scissors]

1036
00:38:43,044 --> 00:38:45,535
[Let's go together, Lee Teuk...!]
Lee Teuk! Lee Teuk!

1037
00:38:45,535 --> 00:38:47,203
[Scissors / Scissors / Rock]
Rock-Paper-Scissors!

1038
00:38:47,203 --> 00:38:48,405
- Ugh!
- Oh!

1039
00:38:48,405 --> 00:38:50,995
[Lee Teuk excluded]
Lee Teuk, step out.

1040
00:38:50,995 --> 00:38:52,744
[DAWN VS Ji Sung]
Shoot or win!

1041
00:38:52,744 --> 00:38:53,655
Rock-Paper-Scissors!

1042
00:38:53,655 --> 00:38:55,508
[Scissors / Rock]

1043
00:38:55,508 --> 00:38:58,229
[Ji Sung wins]
Oh, Ji Sung!

1044
00:38:58,229 --> 00:38:59,255
- I was happy because I won.
- Sorry.

1045
00:38:59,255 --> 00:39:00,359
[The youngest paupers gets the drinks]
Something is going on between us.

1046
00:39:00,359 --> 00:39:01,446
- I was happy I won.
- Let's go.

1047
00:39:01,446 --> 00:39:03,047
Have a good trip!

1048
00:39:04,343 --> 00:39:06,044
- It's us again?
- I know, right?

1049
00:39:06,044 --> 00:39:08,642
- There's a problem with this!
- It's us again.

1050
00:39:08,642 --> 00:39:11,144
I'm used to it.
I have nothing to lose.

1051
00:39:11,144 --> 00:39:12,646
[Enlightenment]
But I've gotten used to it too.

1052
00:39:12,646 --> 00:39:14,460
- Hey, you two, take a seat.
- Oh, can we sit here?

1053
00:39:14,460 --> 00:39:16,337
- Please sit for a moment. Yes.
- Thank you, Your Highness.

1054
00:39:16,337 --> 00:39:17,854
- Please sit for a moment.
- Your Highness.

1055
00:39:17,854 --> 00:39:19,411
[Ahead of the real fun by the pool]
Yes, we…

1056
00:39:19,411 --> 00:39:22,244
Firstly, Lee Teuk, I'm sorry,
but can you check the water temperature?

1057
00:39:22,244 --> 00:39:24,650
Yeah, tell us how the water is.

1058
00:39:31,016 --> 00:39:33,644
- Lee Teuk! You're quite funny!
- Oh, was it funny?

1059
00:39:33,644 --> 00:39:34,456
[Scored 1 point for the slapstick]
Plus 1 point!

1060
00:39:34,456 --> 00:39:35,755
- When you head down…
- Oh, that was funny!

1061
00:39:35,755 --> 00:39:37,543
- Be careful going down.
- Oh, that was funny.

1062
00:39:37,543 --> 00:39:38,642
- It's slippery.
- That was funny.

1063
00:39:38,642 --> 00:39:39,744
It's slippery.

1064
00:39:39,744 --> 00:39:41,044
Wow, I didn't realize
this would be so funny, then…

1065
00:39:41,044 --> 00:39:43,244
DAWN, please check
the water temperature too!

1066
00:39:43,244 --> 00:39:45,344
- How funny will he be?
- It's colder than expected.

1067
00:39:45,344 --> 00:39:46,377
[Check the temperature again...??]
It's colder than expected.

1068
00:39:46,377 --> 00:39:48,321
[LOL]
You have to really check the water temperature, okay?

1069
00:39:48,321 --> 00:39:50,453
[Thermometer DAWN is on the move]
I'll check the water temperature now.

1070
00:39:50,453 --> 00:39:52,551
- Yes, the water temperature.
- Sirs.

1071
00:39:52,551 --> 00:39:55,337
- The water temperature.
- I didn't know you were good at slapstick too.

1072
00:39:55,337 --> 00:39:56,744
Sorry, but...

1073
00:39:56,744 --> 00:39:57,944
- DAWN.
- Yes?

1074
00:39:57,944 --> 00:39:59,945
Your legs are so thin.

1075
00:39:59,945 --> 00:40:01,444
Hey, I found someone
with skinnier legs than mine!

1076
00:40:01,444 --> 00:40:02,844
[The fallen prince's legs]
They look like ostrich legs!

1077
00:40:02,844 --> 00:40:03,980
I might get blown away!

1078
00:40:03,980 --> 00:40:06,243
Let's check the water temperature again.

1079
00:40:06,243 --> 00:40:07,344
[Hesitating]

1080
00:40:07,344 --> 00:40:08,144
The water temperature?

1081
00:40:08,144 --> 00:40:11,588
- Yes, check the water temperature.
- I'm worried he might get blown away!

1082
00:40:11,588 --> 00:40:13,415
[Reading the room]
Please check the water temperature.

1083
00:40:13,415 --> 00:40:14,776
No, but seriously…

1084
00:40:14,776 --> 00:40:16,277
I have to… I have to be funny, right?

1085
00:40:16,277 --> 00:40:17,358
If you're funny, that's extra points.

1086
00:40:17,358 --> 00:40:19,476
If you're funny…!
If you're funny, yes, yes.

1087
00:40:19,476 --> 00:40:20,944
[Determined to be funny]

1088
00:40:20,944 --> 00:40:24,359
- I'll check the temperature, Your Highnesses.
- Please check the water temperature.

1089
00:40:26,510 --> 00:40:28,605
[Temperature check]

1090
00:40:28,605 --> 00:40:30,411
[Nice one, DAWN]

1091
00:40:30,411 --> 00:40:31,543
Wow, that was good!

1092
00:40:31,543 --> 00:40:33,528
- Wow, that was good!
- Oh, totally, totally!

1093
00:40:33,528 --> 00:40:35,263
- How's the water temperature?
- The water temperature is perfect.

1094
00:40:35,263 --> 00:40:36,377
Hey, I wasn't expecting that!

1095
00:40:36,377 --> 00:40:37,716
- How's the water temperature?
- It's just right.

1096
00:40:37,716 --> 00:40:38,944
- It's just right?
- Isn't it a little cold?

1097
00:40:38,944 --> 00:40:40,544
- It's good to go in?
- You can go in.

1098
00:40:40,544 --> 00:40:41,551
[The struggles of the former ALL Prince]
We'll go in after our drinks.

1099
00:40:41,551 --> 00:40:42,743
- Oh, after your drinks.
- Yes, yes.

1100
00:40:42,743 --> 00:40:44,234
- Did I get any bonus points?
- 2 points!!

1101
00:40:44,234 --> 00:40:45,244
- I'll give you 2 points!
- Agreed, agreed!

1102
00:40:45,244 --> 00:40:48,650
- Aw! Me too! Me too!
- I'll give you 2 points.

1103
00:40:48,650 --> 00:40:51,845
[The princes couldn't be more pleased]
But let's make them all do this!

1104
00:40:51,845 --> 00:40:54,197
Oh, that was fun!

1105
00:40:54,197 --> 00:40:55,177
Oh, it was perfect.

1106
00:40:55,177 --> 00:40:59,276
[Lamenting his fate]
Why couldn't I find the caramel?

1107
00:40:59,276 --> 00:41:03,136
[The youngest paupers arrive at the minibar]

1108
00:41:03,136 --> 00:41:05,144
Excuse me.

1109
00:41:05,144 --> 00:41:07,277
[Drink order list]
Zero Coke…

1110
00:41:07,277 --> 00:41:08,544
[Four Zero Cokes]
1, 2, 3, 4.

1111
00:41:08,544 --> 00:41:10,244
Four Zero Cokes.

1112
00:41:10,244 --> 00:41:11,448
- Four?
- Yeah.

1113
00:41:11,448 --> 00:41:14,047
[One Coke]
One Coke with ice.

1114
00:41:14,047 --> 00:41:17,746
[One Iced Americano]
And one iced Americano with ice.

1115
00:41:17,746 --> 00:41:21,152
(Lots of ice)
But the iced Americano is full ice, please.

1116
00:41:21,152 --> 00:41:22,859
[Ordered with lots of ice, without forgetting]
Thank you!

1117
00:41:23,526 --> 00:41:26,138
You two, for 2 points, race there and back.

1118
00:41:26,138 --> 00:41:27,211
Let's see who's faster.

1119
00:41:27,211 --> 00:41:29,428
- Are you a good swimmer??
- I can't swim at all.

1120
00:41:29,428 --> 00:41:31,090
- Oh, not at all?
- Yeah.

1121
00:41:31,090 --> 00:41:32,644
You can just walk it.

1122
00:41:32,644 --> 00:41:34,043
- As long as you make it somehow.
- Yes, yes.

1123
00:41:34,043 --> 00:41:35,711
[Whining]
But it's really cold.

1124
00:41:35,711 --> 00:41:37,651
If you whine about the cold,
that's minus points.

1125
00:41:37,651 --> 00:41:38,642
No, like…

1126
00:41:38,642 --> 00:41:40,611
[Whining...]
We could freeze to death...

1127
00:41:40,611 --> 00:41:42,248
- Lee Teuk.
- Yes?

1128
00:41:43,137 --> 00:41:45,177
[Backing down]
Okay, okay, got it, got it.

1129
00:41:45,177 --> 00:41:47,343
Don't say my name like that…

1130
00:41:47,343 --> 00:41:48,919
- I know I'm Lee Teuk.
- Okay, I'm ready.

1131
00:41:48,919 --> 00:41:51,243
[Stop whining and prepare for the swim battle]
Let's go!

1132
00:41:51,243 --> 00:41:52,444
Do you have a whistle?

1133
00:41:52,444 --> 00:41:55,043
[Proactive since it's the prince's command]
Can you blow it once? You don't have one?

1134
00:41:56,036 --> 00:41:57,994
- Oh, it's cold!
- The shot looks nice!

1135
00:41:57,994 --> 00:41:59,454
- Black and white looks great!
- Yeah.

1136
00:41:59,454 --> 00:42:00,644
[Go stone vibes]
You look like Go stones.

1137
00:42:00,644 --> 00:42:01,962
So cold!

1138
00:42:01,962 --> 00:42:03,064
Ugh! So cold!

1139
00:42:03,064 --> 00:42:04,668
[Whining overload]
It's so cold!

1140
00:42:04,668 --> 00:42:05,566
Is he sneezing?

1141
00:42:05,566 --> 00:42:08,110
[Calm down and come back]
Okay, you two, come this way, and we'll begin.

1142
00:42:08,743 --> 00:42:10,677
Hey, it's way too deep here!!!!

1143
00:42:10,677 --> 00:42:12,668
Try going in once to see how deep it is.

1144
00:42:12,668 --> 00:42:13,661
- Wait a second.
- Yeah?

1145
00:42:13,661 --> 00:42:16,211
[Getting emotional]
We're paupers, but not slaves.

1146
00:42:16,211 --> 00:42:17,811
- Then, you're not gonna do it?
- No, I will, but…

1147
00:42:17,811 --> 00:42:19,144
- You don't have to do it.
- No, I will, but…

1148
00:42:19,144 --> 00:42:21,244
- Lee Teuk! - 10 points!
- No, no, wait, wait!

1149
00:42:21,244 --> 00:42:22,511
Let's talk for a second!

1150
00:42:22,511 --> 00:42:24,211
No, no, no. I'll do it.

1151
00:42:24,211 --> 00:42:25,441
(Desperate)
No, I'll do it, I'll do it.

1152
00:42:25,441 --> 00:42:26,387
Alright, here we go! Ready!

1153
00:42:26,387 --> 00:42:28,450
- Not yet, not yet!
- Stay at the end, at the end!

1154
00:42:28,450 --> 00:42:30,118
Now, ready!

1155
00:42:30,118 --> 00:42:31,856
Wait, hold on!
There's something here!

1156
00:42:31,856 --> 00:42:33,196
There's something here!

1157
00:42:33,196 --> 00:42:34,345
- Ready!!
- Wait!

1158
00:42:34,345 --> 00:42:35,465
Go!

1159
00:42:35,465 --> 00:42:37,597
[The round-trip race begins]
Alright, it's starting!

1160
00:42:38,776 --> 00:42:39,661
[They jump into
the water at the same time]

1161
00:42:39,661 --> 00:42:40,868
- Oh! Oh!
- They're swimming!

1162
00:42:40,868 --> 00:42:41,871
Oh, they're swimming!

1163
00:42:41,871 --> 00:42:44,137
They're both great swimmers.

1164
00:42:45,940 --> 00:42:47,147
Hold on.

1165
00:42:48,176 --> 00:42:51,411
The princes are out of the pool,
and the paupers are swimming…?

1166
00:42:51,411 --> 00:42:53,049
[What is going on??]
This is seriously hilarious.

1167
00:42:53,049 --> 00:42:55,535
They must've been
told to do something.

1168
00:42:55,535 --> 00:42:58,822
[The paupers are having a blast swimming]
You gotta go all the way!

1169
00:42:58,822 --> 00:43:01,776
[Giggles]

1170
00:43:01,776 --> 00:43:05,210
[Advancing toward the finish line]

1171
00:43:05,210 --> 00:43:08,210
[Pauper Lee Teuk is in the lead]

1172
00:43:09,438 --> 00:43:10,731
(Giving up)

1173
00:43:10,731 --> 00:43:11,943
Oh, who will it be?

1174
00:43:11,943 --> 00:43:14,059
[Pauper Lee Teuk arrives]
The winner is…!

1175
00:43:14,059 --> 00:43:17,034
[Lee Teuk wins]
Lee Teuk!!

1176
00:43:17,034 --> 00:43:18,295
Wow, nice!

1177
00:43:19,432 --> 00:43:20,434
Your drinks are here!

1178
00:43:20,434 --> 00:43:22,476
- Oh, the drinks are here! The drinks.
- Yes.

1179
00:43:22,476 --> 00:43:23,926
Come out and have a drink.

1180
00:43:23,926 --> 00:43:25,644
[Jealous]
