1636
00:59:30,065 --> 00:59:32,015
His chopsticks went back and forth 4 times.

1637
00:59:32,015 --> 00:59:33,143
Wasn't it just one bite?

1638
00:59:33,143 --> 00:59:35,711
[Let's look]
Check if there's any left!

1639
00:59:35,711 --> 00:59:37,542
Wow, Ji Sung…

1640
00:59:38,188 --> 00:59:40,137
He left scraps for me…

1641
00:59:40,137 --> 00:59:41,758
[Ji Sung chose instinct]
Oh, he left a lot!

1642
00:59:41,758 --> 00:59:43,756
Oh, he left a lot!

1643
00:59:43,756 --> 00:59:47,856
This is exactly how
I gave my dog her food.

1644
00:59:47,856 --> 00:59:51,322
From what I felt, he was gonna
finish it off, but left some behind.

1645
00:59:52,843 --> 00:59:55,510
[The sun sets before long…]

1646
00:59:59,547 --> 01:00:03,310
[Johnny spots the sunset]
Wow, it's got a soft orange glow, everyone!

1647
01:00:04,028 --> 01:00:06,943
This sunset is seriously gorgeous...

1648
01:00:08,543 --> 01:00:11,943
[The crimson sun dyes the sea]
This view is just stunning right now.

1649
01:00:12,776 --> 01:00:15,476
But I think my face
will definitely end up sunburned.

1650
01:00:19,243 --> 01:00:22,843
[The perfect way
to enjoy an Egyptian sunset]

1651
01:00:28,310 --> 01:00:32,343
[Lathering up nicely until the sun sets]

1652
01:00:35,194 --> 01:00:37,143
[This feels amazing…!]

1653
01:00:37,143 --> 01:00:38,586
It really is nice.

1654
01:00:41,843 --> 01:00:45,077
Alright everyone,
time for an urgent announcement!

1655
01:00:45,077 --> 01:00:47,211
Forget all the points
you've gotten so far!

1656
01:00:47,211 --> 01:00:48,944
Your Highness, what are you talking about?

1657
01:00:48,944 --> 01:00:50,444
I got my butt kicked!

1658
01:00:50,444 --> 01:00:53,576
[Score Reset]
Forget the scores you got up until now.

1659
01:00:53,576 --> 01:00:55,344
From now on, through some games,

1660
01:00:55,344 --> 01:00:58,668
[Mini games with a status upgrade on the line]
you'll get a chance for a status upgrade today!

1661
01:00:58,668 --> 01:01:00,400
So what exactly is this "status upgrade"?

1662
01:01:00,400 --> 01:01:02,030
[Prince Shin Dong's & Prince Johnny's quarters]
There are two rooms right now.

1663
01:01:02,030 --> 01:01:05,477
But the four of you
sleeping outside is something

1664
01:01:05,477 --> 01:01:07,844
- we can't get behind.
- The tent is too small, too.

1665
01:01:07,844 --> 01:01:10,380
- So, we'll pick two people…
- Yes, oh!

1666
01:01:10,380 --> 01:01:13,516
and we'll add an extra bed in our rooms.

1667
01:01:13,516 --> 01:01:16,583
We'll give you a chance
to sleep in there with us.

1668
01:01:16,583 --> 01:01:18,488
You won't be a prince,

1669
01:01:18,488 --> 01:01:19,852
- but below that.
- A commoner below that.

1670
01:01:19,852 --> 01:01:20,944
[A chance to upgrade to commoner status!!]
A commoner level!

1671
01:01:20,944 --> 01:01:23,111
- Around a commoner level.
- Oh, a commoner sounds good.

1672
01:01:23,111 --> 01:01:25,277
We've prepared 4 games to start with.

1673
01:01:25,277 --> 01:01:27,401
The first person to get 2 wins

1674
01:01:27,401 --> 01:01:29,262
will escape being a pauper! Got it?

1675
01:01:29,262 --> 01:01:33,877
"We need to put something
on the line so the paupers will try hard."

1676
01:01:33,877 --> 01:01:36,111
[The two princes, Shin Dong and Johnny,
thought to themselves]

1677
01:01:36,111 --> 01:01:37,951
What kind of fun games are there?

1678
01:01:37,951 --> 01:01:40,844
It might be fun to play
old-school-style games too.

1679
01:01:40,844 --> 01:01:43,444
Should we write down some games
and then choose randomly?

1680
01:01:43,444 --> 01:01:45,577
[A 2nd meeting with the production team]
We're thinking of doing it that way at the end.

1681
01:01:45,577 --> 01:01:49,877
We thought it'd be fun to play games
and save two people.

1682
01:01:49,877 --> 01:01:53,144
Whether it's written on paper or on chopsticks,
so they can pick them randomly.

1683
01:01:53,144 --> 01:01:55,911
Since this was my first chance
to escape being a pauper,

1684
01:01:55,911 --> 01:01:57,944
I knew I had to give it my all!
I just had to do it!

1685
01:01:57,944 --> 01:01:59,277
I loved it!

1686
01:01:59,277 --> 01:02:02,844
[Today's Mini Game]
[Paupers' Talent Show]

1687
01:02:02,844 --> 01:02:05,168
[Today's Game]
The first game will be the Apartment Game!

1688
01:02:05,168 --> 01:02:06,736
[Going beyond K-drinking games,]
APT. APT.

1689
01:02:06,736 --> 01:02:08,211
[the game that caused a global phenomenon]
APT. APT.

1690
01:02:08,211 --> 01:02:09,744
[After randomly stacking both hands,]
13th floor! You know, right?

1691
01:02:09,744 --> 01:02:11,544
[move the hand at the bottom to the top]
The person who falls on the number!

1692
01:02:11,544 --> 01:02:13,711
[Land on the number that's called and you're out!]
The one who falls on it!

1693
01:02:13,711 --> 01:02:16,644
The last person standing gets 1 point.

1694
01:02:16,644 --> 01:02:17,877
The last person gets 1 point.

1695
01:02:17,877 --> 01:02:19,244
[Must avoid the apartment floor that's called!]
If you get caught on the number, you're out!

1696
01:02:19,244 --> 01:02:20,477
- Oh, if you get caught, you're out. Okay!
- Got it?

1697
01:02:20,477 --> 01:02:21,844
[Emphasizing once more]
The last person remaining gets 1 point.

1698
01:02:21,844 --> 01:02:22,744
The last person remaining gets 1 point.

1699
01:02:22,744 --> 01:02:24,944
And then the second game! The Shoe Toss!

1700
01:02:24,944 --> 01:02:27,237
[From the starting line, kick your shoe]
You'll kick off your own shoe.

1701
01:02:27,237 --> 01:02:28,944
[The person whose shoe lands]
We'll mark a line.

1702
01:02:28,944 --> 01:02:30,252
[the closest to the finish line wins!]
The shoe that lands closest to the line wins!

1703
01:02:30,252 --> 01:02:32,243
[Over the line, and you're out!]
If it goes over the line, you're out!

1704
01:02:32,243 --> 01:02:34,253
Next is the Standing Long Jump!

1705
01:02:34,253 --> 01:02:36,477
- Oh, Standing Long Jump.
- Standing Long Jump.

1706
01:02:36,477 --> 01:02:39,344
The last game is I Came Alone!

1707
01:02:39,344 --> 01:02:40,528
[Matching the number of your turn,]
"I came alone,"

1708
01:02:40,528 --> 01:02:42,117
[shout out "I came alone!" "We came as a pair!"]
"We came as a pair," "We came as a trio"…

1709
01:02:42,117 --> 01:02:44,126
[The repeating pattern]
1-2-3-3-2-1.

1710
01:02:44,126 --> 01:02:45,836
- We'll go in this order.
- Oh, this is hard, this is hard.

1711
01:02:45,836 --> 01:02:48,044
- You all got it?
- I'm really bad at things like this.

1712
01:02:48,044 --> 01:02:50,210
[Take care of the youngest]
Wrap the towel around Ji Sung. It's cold.

1713
01:02:50,981 --> 01:02:52,916
I don't know how to wrap this.

1714
01:02:52,916 --> 01:02:54,171
You can't wrap it yourself?

1715
01:02:54,171 --> 01:02:55,952
[To raise the youngest,]
Just tie it. Tie the front here.

1716
01:02:55,952 --> 01:02:56,952
[it takes a whole village]
And then tuck it in.

1717
01:02:56,952 --> 01:02:59,242
- You have to tie it. Tie it.
- Got it, got it!

1718
01:02:59,242 --> 01:03:02,840
[Random draw for the first game]
Let's see what the first game will be.

1719
01:03:02,840 --> 01:03:04,764
Johnny will draw it!

1720
01:03:04,764 --> 01:03:06,258
[Pull]
Alright, the first game is…!

1721
01:03:06,258 --> 01:03:08,133
[First game]
It's Apartment!

1722
01:03:08,133 --> 01:03:09,039
- Wow!
- Nice!

1723
01:03:09,039 --> 01:03:10,577
♪ APT. APT. ♪

1724
01:03:10,577 --> 01:03:12,047
[A game that sets a hyped vibe]
♪ APT. APT. ♪

1725
01:03:12,047 --> 01:03:14,911
♪ APT. APT.
Uh, uh huh uh huh! ♪

1726
01:03:14,911 --> 01:03:16,744
[The princes decide which apartment floor]
We'll call out the apartment floor!

1727
01:03:16,744 --> 01:03:18,644
[The paupers will]
We'll take turns calling out the floors.

1728
01:03:18,644 --> 01:03:20,477
[stack their hands to the intro beat]
You have to put both hands in.

1729
01:03:20,477 --> 01:03:21,811
[APT. Round 1]
5, 6, 7, 8!

1730
01:03:21,811 --> 01:03:24,611
♪ APT. APT. APT. APT. ♪

1731
01:03:24,611 --> 01:03:25,844
♪ APT. APT. ♪

1732
01:03:25,844 --> 01:03:27,111
- 1st floor!
- 1st floor!

1733
01:03:27,111 --> 01:03:28,111
1st floor?

1734
01:03:28,111 --> 01:03:31,344
- It's me!
- 1st floor!

1735
01:03:31,344 --> 01:03:33,344
If you get caught on it, you're out!

1736
01:03:33,344 --> 01:03:35,121
Okay, 3 people left!

1737
01:03:35,121 --> 01:03:36,311
- The last one standing wins!
- If you get caught, you're eliminated.

1738
01:03:36,311 --> 01:03:38,795
- Weren't we supposed to get caught?
- No, you're out.

1739
01:03:38,795 --> 01:03:40,493
- You should've told me!
- I did!

1740
01:03:40,493 --> 01:03:41,541
When did you say that?!

1741
01:03:41,541 --> 01:03:43,998
The last person standing…!

1742
01:03:43,998 --> 01:03:47,011
- I said it!
- This is just a practice game.

1743
01:03:47,011 --> 01:03:48,644
[Tossed aside]
I told you.

1744
01:03:48,644 --> 01:03:50,544
[APT. ROUND 2]
Now, Johnny will call it!

1745
01:03:50,544 --> 01:03:51,977
5, 6, 7, 8!

1746
01:03:51,977 --> 01:03:54,611
♪ APT. APT. APT. APT. ♪

1747
01:03:54,611 --> 01:03:55,844
- 10!
- 10th floor!

1748
01:03:55,844 --> 01:03:56,744
1!

1749
01:03:56,744 --> 01:03:57,444
2!

1750
01:03:57,444 --> 01:03:58,111
3!

1751
01:03:58,111 --> 01:03:58,711
4!

1752
01:03:58,711 --> 01:03:59,249
5!

1753
01:03:59,249 --> 01:03:59,811
6!

1754
01:03:59,811 --> 01:04:00,477
7!

1755
01:04:00,477 --> 01:04:00,910
8!

1756
01:04:00,910 --> 01:04:01,577
9!

1757
01:04:01,577 --> 01:04:03,086
10!

1758
01:04:03,086 --> 01:04:05,744
[Yo Han gets the 10th-floor-apartment]
10!

1759
01:04:05,744 --> 01:04:08,455
[An elaborate ceremony for their eliminated pauper bro]
Alright, down to 2 people!

1760
01:04:08,455 --> 01:04:10,311
- Okay, I'll call it now!
- Hey, one more time!

1761
01:04:10,311 --> 01:04:12,277
This game's fun!
Let's play it one more time!

1762
01:04:12,277 --> 01:04:14,077
[APT. Finals]
5, 6, 7, 8!

1763
01:04:14,077 --> 01:04:16,677
♪ APT. APT. APT. APT. ♪

1764
01:04:16,677 --> 01:04:17,744
17th floor!

1765
01:04:17,744 --> 01:04:18,944
- Oh, like this!
- Heading up to the 17th floor!

1766
01:04:18,944 --> 01:04:20,277
1! 2!

1767
01:04:20,277 --> 01:04:21,277
3! 4!

1768
01:04:21,277 --> 01:04:22,377
5! 6!

1769
01:04:22,377 --> 01:04:23,644
[The floors climb higher]
7! 8!

1770
01:04:23,644 --> 01:04:24,544
9! 10!

1771
01:04:24,544 --> 01:04:25,444
11! 12!

1772
01:04:25,444 --> 01:04:26,244
13! 14!

1773
01:04:26,244 --> 01:04:27,340
15! 16!

1774
01:04:27,340 --> 01:04:30,211
[DAWN's out on the 17th floor!]
- 17! - Out!

1775
01:04:30,211 --> 01:04:33,244
[Ji Sung scores 1 point in the first game!]
Ji Sung gets 1 point!

1776
01:04:33,244 --> 01:04:35,144
- Hey, this game's fun!
- Hey, this is so fun!

1777
01:04:35,144 --> 01:04:36,644
[So close!]

1778
01:04:36,644 --> 01:04:38,944
[Objection]
Usually, getting caught is a good thing.

1779
01:04:38,944 --> 01:04:40,844
- Right, usually getting caught is a good thing.
- Ji Sung gets 1 point.

1780
01:04:40,844 --> 01:04:42,425
- Why didn't you say getting caught equals out?
- I did say it.

1781
01:04:42,425 --> 01:04:43,393
[Announced it from the start]
When did you say that?

1782
01:04:43,393 --> 01:04:44,895
- I said it at the beginning.
- Oh, really?

1783
01:04:44,895 --> 01:04:46,444
[He explained it nicely]
The last person remaining gets 1 point.

1784
01:04:46,444 --> 01:04:47,755
If you get caught on the number, you're out!

1785
01:04:47,755 --> 01:04:49,048
- Oh, if you get caught, you're out. Okay!
- Got it?

1786
01:04:49,048 --> 01:04:50,211
The last person gets 1 point.

1787
01:04:50,211 --> 01:04:52,911
Now, the second game! Johnny will pick!

1788
01:04:52,911 --> 01:04:55,344
Ji Sung, which one do you want?

1789
01:04:55,344 --> 01:04:56,311
The one on the right!

1790
01:04:56,311 --> 01:04:57,541
[Random pick:
Chose the chopstick on the far right!]

1791
01:04:57,541 --> 01:04:59,235
- Please!
- What is it?

1792
01:04:59,235 --> 01:05:00,777
- Please!
- What is it?

1793
01:05:00,777 --> 01:05:03,411
[Second game]
The Shoe Toss!

1794
01:05:03,411 --> 01:05:05,310
There's a headwind.

1795
01:05:05,310 --> 01:05:06,977
[Mania]
Can't we play Apartment again?

1796
01:05:06,977 --> 01:05:08,014
Apartment's fun, right?

1797
01:05:08,014 --> 01:05:09,849
Apartment's the best!

1798
01:05:09,849 --> 01:05:12,455
[Deciding the shoe-tossing order]
Everyone, let's do Rock-Paper-Scissors for the order.

1799
01:05:12,455 --> 01:05:15,828
Shoot or lose!
Rock-Paper-Scissors!

1800
01:05:15,828 --> 01:05:16,944
Rock-Paper-Scissors!

1801
01:05:16,944 --> 01:05:18,476
Rock-Paper-Scissors!
Oh, okay!

1802
01:05:18,476 --> 01:05:19,743
- Ji Sung, decide the order!
- Oh, I'm first.

1803
01:05:19,743 --> 01:05:20,959
[1st place Ji Sung decides the order]
1st place chooses the order!

1804
01:05:20,959 --> 01:05:22,344
Oh okay, then…

1805
01:05:22,344 --> 01:05:24,444
- 1st place, you decide it.
- I will…

1806
01:05:24,444 --> 01:05:25,744
I will go by age order!

1807
01:05:25,744 --> 01:05:27,054
Alright, everyone!

1808
01:05:27,054 --> 01:05:28,544
[From youngest to oldest]
Starting with me!

1809
01:05:28,544 --> 01:05:30,854
- Oh, you first!
- Let me explain the rules.

1810
01:05:30,854 --> 01:05:33,377
If you're on the line, you're out.

1811
01:05:33,377 --> 01:05:37,144
[The shoe closest to the line wins]
Whoever's shoe is closest to the line wins.

1812
01:05:37,144 --> 01:05:39,136
- Can we go past it?
- If your shoe crosses it, you're out.

1813
01:05:39,136 --> 01:05:40,577
- Got it, got it.
- You all got it, right?

1814
01:05:40,577 --> 01:05:41,677
It's okay to be on the line?

1815
01:05:41,677 --> 01:05:43,344
You can't be on the line.
If you're on the line, you're out!

1816
01:05:43,344 --> 01:05:44,044
Oh, really?

1817
01:05:44,044 --> 01:05:46,043
But is it better to
go later in the order here?

1818
01:05:46,543 --> 01:05:49,709
[Lee Teuk's quick practice]

1819
01:05:50,103 --> 01:05:51,616
[The princes set up
the game for the paupers]

1820
01:05:51,616 --> 01:05:52,977
- It was a boomerang!
- Hey, this is fun!

1821
01:05:52,977 --> 01:05:55,210
Hey Shin Dong, check this out!

1822
01:05:56,476 --> 01:05:59,744
[Thanks to the Red Sea breeze,
boomerang slippers are a thing]

1823
01:05:59,744 --> 01:06:02,277
[They must get close to the rope line]
We have the rope line here!

1824
01:06:02,277 --> 01:06:04,344
Since you have two shoes,
you'll get two chances!

1825
01:06:04,344 --> 01:06:05,344
- Oh!
- Oh, two chances each.

1826
01:06:05,344 --> 01:06:06,944
[Player 1: Ji Sung]
Here we go!

1827
01:06:06,944 --> 01:06:08,859
Ready, start!

1828
01:06:12,011 --> 01:06:13,045
- Out!
- Out!

1829
01:06:13,045 --> 01:06:14,744
[Ji Sung is out, just like that]

1830
01:06:14,744 --> 01:06:17,011
[You'd think it was a long-distance shoe-toss]
You kicked it ridiculously far.

1831
01:06:17,011 --> 01:06:18,034
Oh, but…

1832
01:06:18,034 --> 01:06:19,135
Ji Sung, out!

1833
01:06:19,135 --> 01:06:21,163
[Just as Ji Sung was about to throw it,]
The wind suddenly stopped blowing.

1834
01:06:21,163 --> 01:06:22,192
[the wind suddenly stopped]
Exactly.

1835
01:06:22,192 --> 01:06:24,057
- Ji Sung's out! Next round!
- This is so unfair.

1836
01:06:24,057 --> 01:06:26,029
Yo Han's up!

1837
01:06:26,029 --> 01:06:28,363
[How are Athletic Yo Han's]
Ready!

1838
01:06:28,363 --> 01:06:30,067
[shoe-tossing skills?]
Go!

1839
01:06:31,337 --> 01:06:32,948
Wait!

1840
01:06:33,647 --> 01:06:34,950
(Plop)
Wait!

1841
01:06:34,950 --> 01:06:36,011
Oh, here! Here!

1842
01:06:36,011 --> 01:06:37,344
[Yo Han, you seriously belong on variety shows]
Here, here, here!

1843
01:06:37,344 --> 01:06:38,645
- No, right here, right here!
- No, my foot got stuck!

1844
01:06:38,645 --> 01:06:39,611
- Right here, right here!
- My foot got stuck!

1845
01:06:39,611 --> 01:06:40,556
- It's right here!
- Seriously!

1846
01:06:40,556 --> 01:06:42,828
[Buried]
Yo Han's so funny! What do I do?

1847
01:06:42,828 --> 01:06:43,744
Alright, Yo Han's here.

1848
01:06:43,744 --> 01:06:46,444
[Amazingly enough, Yo Han's in 1st place]
You never know. You could get 1st place!

1849
01:06:46,444 --> 01:06:47,463
[Just need to pass this point]
You could get 1st place.

1850
01:06:47,463 --> 01:06:49,776
[Player 3: DAWN]
Now!

1851
01:06:50,551 --> 01:06:51,976
He looks like an eagle.

1852
01:06:51,976 --> 01:06:53,089
[Great energy!]
Alright, nice!

1853
01:06:53,089 --> 01:06:55,312
- Good, good.
- Here goes DAWN! DAWN!

1854
01:06:56,010 --> 01:06:57,343
Here I go!

1855
01:06:57,776 --> 01:06:59,276
[Hyah!]

1856
01:06:59,743 --> 01:07:00,776
(Zoom)

1857
01:07:01,197 --> 01:07:02,432
[Currently 1st place: DAWN]
Right here!

1858
01:07:02,432 --> 01:07:03,544
[Nice shoe toss]
Here, here.

1859
01:07:03,544 --> 01:07:06,077
- I'll tone down the comedy a bit.
- Yes.

1860
01:07:06,077 --> 01:07:07,944
- I'll focus on winning first!
- Sounds good, sounds good!

1861
01:07:07,944 --> 01:07:09,111
Then I should go
with a strategic approach.

1862
01:07:09,111 --> 01:07:10,544
[Lee Teuk's special toes]
Oh, the toes!

1863
01:07:10,544 --> 01:07:12,044
Oh, the toes are good!

1864
